window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"u":"index.html","p":"Welcome","s":"Free GST Billing documentation","t":"Make GST invoices, keep track of who owes you, and prepare your GST returns. On your own computer, with no account and no monthly fee."},{"u":"index.html#what-it-does","p":"Welcome","s":"What it does","t":"what-it-does\"> Free GST Billing is invoicing and GST software for small businesses in India, and for anyone billing in other currencies: 20 are supported. It runs on your computer and opens in your web browser, the way a website does, but nothing leaves your machine. Invoices : tax invoices, bills of supply, proforma estimates, credit notes and delivery challans, with CGST, SGST, IGST and UTGST worked out for you. Getting paid : record payments, print receipts, see who is overdue and by how much. GST returns : GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B built from your invoices and purchases, as files you upload to th"},{"u":"index.html#requirements","p":"Welcome","s":"What you need","t":"requirements\"> Computer Windows 10 or 11, macOS, or Linux (a NAS works too). Browser Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Brave. The app opens in it. Disk space Roughly 200 MB once installed. Internet Only for the first install and for updates. Everything else works offline. Account or signup None."},{"u":"index.html#your-data","p":"Welcome","s":"Where your data lives","t":"your-data\"> Every invoice, client and setting is saved as plain files inside the app's folder, in _system\\data . They never leave your computer unless you turn on Google Drive backup yourself. That also means backing up is your job, and it is easy. See Backups, updates and moving PC ."},{"u":"index.html#is-it-free","p":"Welcome","s":"Is it really free?","t":"is-it-free\"> Yes. It is open source under the MIT licence. There is no trial, no invoice limit, no feature that unlocks for money, and no advertising. The code is public on GitHub , so anyone can check what it does."},{"u":"index.html#get-help","p":"Welcome","s":"Getting help","t":"get-help\"> Every screen in the app with a ? button links to the matching part of these pages. If something is missing here, or the app does something these pages don't describe, open an issue on GitHub with a screenshot. Many features began as someone's request."},{"u":"install.html","p":"Install","s":"Install","t":"Download one ZIP, extract it, open the launcher for your computer and click Install. On Windows it sets up everything it needs by itself."},{"u":"install.html#download","p":"Install","s":"Download","t":"download\"> Download the ZIP. The link always gives you the newest version. Download Free GST Billing Use this link, not GitHub's green Code button The green Code button on GitHub gives you the source code, not the app. It will not install."},{"u":"install.html#windows","p":"Install","s":"Install on Windows","t":"windows\"> Extract the ZIP Right-click the downloaded file and choose Extract All… , then Extract . Put it somewhere you will remember, such as Documents . Open the launcher In the new folder, double-click Free GST Billing - WINDOWS . Each launcher is named after the computer it is for. Click Install A small window opens with one button. Click Install . There is nothing to fill in. Wait for the browser A black window does the work and closes by itself. It takes one to three minutes the first time. The app then opens in your browser at http://localhost:47371 . Before install, the launcher shows "},{"u":"install.html#extract-first","p":"Install","s":"Extract the ZIP before opening anything","t":"extract-first\"> Windows lets you double-click a file while you are still looking inside a ZIP. When you do, it copies just that one file to a temporary folder and runs it there, so the rest of the app is not next to it. The launcher notices this and says Please extract the ZIP first , with a button that opens your Downloads folder. Close it, extract the ZIP, and open the launcher from the extracted folder."},{"u":"install.html#windows-protected","p":"Install","s":"\"Windows protected your PC\"","t":"windows-protected\"> You may see this blue warning the first time. It appears for software that is not signed with a paid certificate, which costs a few hundred dollars a year and would make a free app not free. Click More info . Click Run anyway . If the file will not open at all, right-click Free GST Billing - WINDOWS , choose Properties , tick Unblock at the bottom, and click OK . If your antivirus removes a file during install, add the app's folder to its exclusions and click Install again."},{"u":"install.html#what-install-does","p":"Install","s":"What the installer does","t":"what-install-does\"> Sets up Node.js inside the app folder , if your PC does not already have it. Node.js is the engine the app runs on. It is downloaded once (about 30 MB) from nodejs.org and kept in _system\\node . Nothing is installed into Windows, and no administrator rights are needed. Downloads the app's building blocks from the internet. This is the only other download. Puts a Free GST Billing shortcut on your Desktop and in the Start menu, with the app's icon. Opens the app in your browser when it is done. If you already have Node.js, the installer uses yours and leaves it alone."},{"u":"install.html#one-command","p":"Install","s":"Install with one command (optional)","t":"one-command\"> If you are comfortable with a terminal, this does all of the above. Open PowerShell and paste: irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OmRaj6666/GST-Billing-Software-LIFE-TIME-USE-NO-Subscription-Required-/main/install.ps1 | iex It installs to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Free GST Billing . To choose another folder, run this first: $env:FREEGSTBILL_DIR = 'D:\\Apps\\Free GST Billing' If the app is already installed in that folder with data in it, the command stops and tells you to update from inside the app instead, so it can never write over your books."},{"u":"install.html#mac","p":"Install","s":"Install on a Mac","t":"mac\"> On a Mac, Node.js has to be installed first. It is free. Install Node.js Download the installer from nodejs.org , or if you use Homebrew, run brew install node@20 . Extract the ZIP Double-click the downloaded ZIP. macOS extracts it next to the download. Open the launcher In the folder, open Free GST Billing - MAC . If macOS says it is from an unidentified developer, right-click it, choose Open , then Open again. Let it finish A Terminal window sets the app up the first time, then opens it in your browser."},{"u":"install.html#linux","p":"Install","s":"Install on Linux or a NAS","t":"linux\"> As on a Mac, install Node.js 18 or newer first, for example sudo apt install nodejs npm . Then: unzip Free-GST-Billing.zip cd Free-GST-Billing chmod +x \"Free GST Billing - LINUX.sh\" ./\"Free GST Billing - LINUX.sh\" The app then runs at http://localhost:47371 . To update later from inside the app, the system also needs unzip or python3."},{"u":"install.html#first-run","p":"Install","s":"The first time the app opens","t":"first-run\"> A short welcome asks for your business details and bank or UPI, then offers to set up your invoices for your kind of business. See The first-run setup ."},{"u":"install.html#open-daily","p":"Install","s":"Opening the app every day","t":"open-daily\"> Double-click the Free GST Billing shortcut on your Desktop, then Open App . The launcher is also where you update, back up, restore, and move to another PC, under More options . Keep the launcher It is the one file you need. You never have to download anything again to update; the launcher does it for you."},{"u":"install.html#uninstall","p":"Install","s":"Removing the app","t":"uninstall\"> Nothing is installed into Windows itself, so removing the app is just deleting it: Back up your data first if you might want it again. See Export everything to one file . In the launcher, open More options and click Stop the app . Delete the app's folder, and the Free GST Billing shortcuts on the Desktop and in the Start menu."},{"u":"first-run.html","p":"First-run setup","s":"The first-run setup","t":"The screens you see the first time the app opens: a four-step welcome for your business details, then a three-step setup for how your invoices look. Both can be skipped and changed later."},{"u":"first-run.html#welcome","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 1 of the welcome: where you invoice from","t":"welcome\"> The first screen explains what the app does, and asks Where will you be invoicing from? 🇮🇳 India GST, GSTR-1 and 3B, UPI. The default. 🌍 Outside India VAT and other local taxes 🌐 Both India, with clients abroad Get Started carries on. Skip Setup goes straight to the app; fill in Settings later."},{"u":"first-run.html#business-details","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 2: business details","t":"business-details\"> These print at the top of every invoice. Only the Business Name is required. Business Name Required Address Your full address State Needed to work out CGST and SGST versus IGST GSTIN Leave blank if you are not registered PAN, Phone, Email Optional"},{"u":"first-run.html#bank-upi","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 3: bank and UPI","t":"bank-upi\"> Where clients should pay you: bank name, account number, IFSC code and UPI ID. A UPI ID puts a scan-to-pay QR code on your invoices. You can also upload your logo and signature here, up to 500 KB each. Skip, I’ll add later leaves it all for Settings ."},{"u":"first-run.html#all-set","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 4: you're all set","t":"all-set\"> A short list of what to do next. Start Billing saves everything; your bank details become your first payment account ."},{"u":"first-run.html#setup-wizard","p":"First-run setup","s":"Then: setting up your invoices","t":"setup-wizard\"> Next, a three-step window sets up printing. What kind of business do you run? Pick one of six: Retail Shop / Kirana, Freelancer / Consultant, Restaurant / Cafe / Bar, Wholesale / Trading, Manufacturing, or Service / Repair Shop. Each sets the invoice style, receipt options and features that suit that business. See Business type for exactly what each one sets. Or choose None of these to set things up yourself. Paper size and language Pick what you mostly print on: A4, A5, 80 mm or 58 mm thermal. It becomes the paper size of new invoices. Then the language for section labels such "},{"u":"first-invoice.html","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Your first invoice","t":"From a blank app to a GST tax invoice you can send, in about five minutes."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#before-you-start","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Before you start","t":"before-you-start\"> Have these to hand: your business name, address and GSTIN, and your bank account or UPI ID if you want clients to pay you directly from the invoice. None of it is compulsory, and all of it can be added later."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#walkthrough","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Make the invoice","t":"walkthrough\"> Add your business details If you skipped the welcome, open Settings and fill in Company Details . This is the header of every invoice. Your state matters: it decides whether GST is split into CGST and SGST, or charged as IGST. Start a new invoice Click New Invoice in the sidebar. Tax Invoice is already selected, which is the right choice for a normal GST sale. Add the client Under Billed To , type the client's name. If they are registered for GST, type their GSTIN and their state fills in by itself. A mistyped GSTIN is caught straight away. Add what you sold For each line, give a"},{"u":"first-invoice.html#send","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Send it","t":"send\"> WhatsApp opens a message to the client. On a phone the PDF is attached for you; on a computer, WhatsApp does not let websites attach files, so download the PDF and drag it into the chat. Print opens your printer directly, including thermal receipt printers. Or attach the downloaded PDF to an email yourself."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#get-paid","p":"Your first invoice","s":"When the client pays","t":"get-paid\"> On the Dashboard , find the invoice and record the payment. A printable receipt opens straight away, and the invoice's status changes to Partial or Paid . Unpaid invoices past their due date are marked Overdue for you."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#whats-next","p":"Your first invoice","s":"What to do next","t":"whats-next\"> Add your products and services , so you pick them from a list instead of typing them each time. Add your bank or UPI , so a payment QR code prints on every invoice. Add your logo, signature and stamp . At the end of the month, prepare your GST returns from the invoices you have made. The Getting started list on the Dashboard tracks these for you, and ticks each one off once it is done."},{"u":"invoices.html","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Making an invoice","t":"Every part of the New Invoice screen, from top to bottom: the toolbar, the document type, the client, the items, terms, extra pages, and what happens when you save, print or share."},{"u":"invoices.html#screen-layout","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How the screen is laid out","t":"screen-layout\"> Open it with New Invoice in the sidebar, or Ctrl + N . The form is on the left and a live preview of the printed invoice is on the right. From top to bottom, the form has these cards: Invoice Type , with the Customize panel when it is open Billed To : the client Invoice Details : number, dates, place of supply and delivery address Line Items Terms & Conditions , notes and a private note Additional Pages / Sections The totals are not in the form. They are worked out as you type and shown in the preview. The invoice screen: the form on the left, the live preview on the right."},{"u":"invoices.html#toolbar","p":"Making an invoice","s":"The toolbar","t":"toolbar\"> The toolbar stays at the top of the screen as you scroll. Button What it does ← Back Leaves the invoice. If you have changed something that is not saved, you are asked first (see Leaving with unsaved changes ). ? A short how-to for this screen. Save status Shows Draft - click to complete until the invoice has a client and an item (click it to jump to what is missing), then Not saved yet until you first save it, then Saving… , All changes saved or Ready . Save Saves the invoice without making a PDF. Ctrl + S does the same. Save & Download Saves the invoice and downloads the PDF. See S"},{"u":"invoices.html#invoice-types","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Choosing the document type","t":"invoice-types\"> The six chips at the top decide the printed title, whether GST is charged, and whether the document counts as a sale in your totals and returns. Type Prints as Use it for GST Counts as a sale? Tax Invoice TAX INVOICE A normal sale by a GST-registered business Yes Yes Quotation QUOTATION A priced offer for work or supply, numbered QUO/…. Convert it to a tax invoice when the client accepts. Shown No Proforma / Estimate PROFORMA INVOICE A quote before the sale. Prints \"This is not a tax invoice\" and a faint ESTIMATE watermark. Shown No Bill of Supply (No GST) BILL OF SUPPLY Exempt"},{"u":"invoices.html#goods-services","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Goods, services or both","t":"goods-services\"> Under the type chips, This invoice is for sets which units you are offered: 📦 Goods Units such as Nos, Kg and Pcs. The default. ⏱ Services Hours, sessions, visits and months. It also reminds you to put a SAC code in the HSN field. 🔀 Mixed Every unit, unfiltered."},{"u":"invoices.html#client","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Billed To: the client","t":"client\"> Type the name Clicking Client Name lists your saved clients. As you type, the list narrows. Use ↓ ↑ and Enter , or click one. Picking a saved client fills in all their details. Or save a new one For someone new, type their name and fill in the fields, then click Save \"name\" as new client to keep them for next time. You do not have to: an invoice can go to a name that is not saved. Check the address and GSTIN Address, country, city, PIN, state and GSTIN print on the invoice. A saved client's pencil icon opens their details for editing. Their email, phone and SEZ setting are only edited"},{"u":"invoices.html#gstin-check","p":"Making an invoice","s":"What the GSTIN check tells you","t":"gstin-check\"> When you leave the GSTIN box, the app reads the number. This works offline, with no GST portal lookup. Message Meaning ✓ Registered in state . State filled in. The state was blank, so it has been filled in from the first two digits. ✓ Registered in state . The GSTIN and the state agree. ⚠ This GSTIN is registered in state , but the state says other state . Check which is right. The tax split follows the state and place of supply. ⚠ This GSTIN fails its own checksum. Check for a typo. Every GSTIN ends with a check character. This one does not add up, so a character is almost certa"},{"u":"invoices.html#client-credit","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Using a client's credit","t":"client-credit\"> If the client overpaid on earlier invoices, a banner shows how much credit they have and where it came from. On a new invoice you can: type an amount to use, or click Apply full to use as much as this invoice needs; click Skip to use none; tick Auto-apply available client credit on future invoices to have it used automatically. When you save, the credit is recorded as a payment on this invoice."},{"u":"invoices.html#details","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Invoice Details","t":"details\"> Field What to know Invoice Number Filled in with the next number for this type. It is only taken when you first save, so an invoice you abandon does not use up a number. If someone else's invoice took it meanwhile, yours gets the next free number and you are told. See Invoice number format . Invoice Date Today, unless you change it. Due Date Blank unless you set it. Once it passes, an unpaid invoice becomes Overdue . Place of Supply Where the goods or services are supplied. Leave it on Defaults to Client State unless the delivery is in a different state from the client's address. The"},{"u":"invoices.html#order-details","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Order, dispatch and reference details","t":"order-details\"> Under Invoice Details, Order, dispatch & reference details opens a set of optional fields, the boxes a Tally invoice carries: work details, revision no, vehicle no, service period from and to, buyer's order no and order date, reference no & date, other references, delivery note and its date, dispatch doc no, dispatched through, destination, mode or terms of payment, and terms of delivery. Only what you fill in prints. The Tally style design shows them in its reference boxes; the other designs list them under Bill To. The section stays open on an invoice that has any of them."},{"u":"invoices.html#items","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Line items","t":"items\"> Each row has these fields: Field What to know Description The item name. Typing searches your products by name or HSN; picking one fills in the HSN, rate, unit and GST rate, and links the row to the product so its stock is counted. HSN/SAC For common codes the app knows the usual GST rate, and shows it in green under the box. If the row's rate is still 18% or 0%, it is changed to match. Qty 1 to start. Clicking the box selects the number, so typing replaces it. Unit From the list for Goods, Services or Mixed. ＋ Add custom… adds your own unit (up to 20 characters), marked ★, and − Remov"},{"u":"invoices.html#tax-inclusive","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Prices that already include GST","t":"tax-inclusive\"> If your rates already include GST, tick Prices include tax at the top of the Line Items card. The printed Subtotal is then the value before tax, so Subtotal + tax = Total. The GST is then worked out backwards from each rate, and the invoice shows the taxable value and the tax separately."},{"u":"invoices.html#discounts","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Discounts","t":"discounts\"> On a line : in the row's Discount box, as described above. This is the GST-correct way, because the discount comes off before tax. On the whole bill : Discount on total , under the items, as an amount or a percentage. It is taken off after tax, so it does not reduce the GST."},{"u":"invoices.html#gst","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How GST is worked out","t":"gst\"> You never choose between CGST, SGST and IGST. The app decides from your state and the place of supply: Situation Charged as Client in your state CGST + SGST, half each Client in another state IGST Within a Union Territory without a legislature (Chandigarh, Ladakh, Lakshadweep, Andaman and Nicobar, Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu) CGST + UTGST SEZ client, or a client outside India IGST The preview shows Intrastate (CGST + SGST) or Interstate (IGST) next to the place of supply, so you can check it before saving. Your own state must be set If your business state is blank in Setting"},{"u":"invoices.html#reverse-charge","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Reverse charge","t":"reverse-charge\"> When the buyer pays the GST instead of you, under section 9(3) or 9(4), open Customize and tick Reverse Charge applies under Compliance flags. The invoice then says Reverse Charge: Yes and prints a notice that the recipient pays the GST. Every tax invoice and credit note prints Reverse Charge Yes or No, as the rules require."},{"u":"invoices.html#tds-tcs","p":"Making an invoice","s":"TDS and TCS","t":"tds-tcs\"> Both are under Customize , for Indian businesses. Turn on TDS / TCS on invoices in Settings, Modules first; it is off to begin with. TCS , tax you collect: tick it and pick the section: CGST section 52 (1%, e-commerce operators), 206C(1), or a custom rate. TCS is added to the invoice total. Section 206C(1H), TCS on sale of goods, was removed from 1 April 2025, so new invoices cannot choose it; invoices already made with it keep it. TDS , tax your client deducts: tick it and pick the section, such as 194Q, 194C, 194J, 194I, 194H, 194O or 195. It is for information: the invoice shows L"},{"u":"invoices.html#currency","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Billing in another currency","t":"currency\"> Under Customize , Currency offers 20 currencies, each with its own symbol and amount in words. For anything other than rupees you can enter the exchange rate for the day. It is kept with the invoice, so later reports stay right even when rates change, and it prints as an EXCHANGE RATE line. The UPI QR code only prints on rupee invoices."},{"u":"invoices.html#terms-notes","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Terms, notes and a private note","t":"terms-notes\"> Terms & Conditions : a text box with B , I , U , bulleted and numbered lists, headings, links and ✕ to clear formatting. Insert preset fills in starter wording for your kind of business: generic trader, freelancer, manufacturer or wholesaler, retail shop, restaurant, IT services, construction, medical, education and coaching, transport, real estate and rental, e-commerce seller, or export under LUT. If you already have terms, you are asked once before they are replaced. Load saved template uses one of your saved templates . On a new invoice, your first template is loaded automati"},{"u":"invoices.html#extra-pages","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Extra pages","t":"extra-pages\"> Under Additional Pages / Sections , + Add Section adds a titled section, such as a scope of work or delivery timeline. Each one prints as its own page after the invoice. You can paste formatted text, lists and tables from Word or Google Docs, and use the arrows to change the order."},{"u":"invoices.html#preview","p":"Making an invoice","s":"The live preview","t":"preview\"> The preview shows the invoice exactly as it will print, with the paper size, style and options you chose. − and + zoom out and in from 50% to 200%, and Fit fits it to the space. A saved invoice that has been cancelled shows CANCELLED across it."},{"u":"invoices.html#before-saving","p":"Making an invoice","s":"What must be filled in","t":"before-saving\"> A new invoice needs a client name and at least one item with a description, quantity and rate. Otherwise Save , Save & Download and Print tell you what is missing."},{"u":"invoices.html#save-download","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Save & Download","t":"save-download\"> Save & Download does all of this in one go: Saves the invoice, giving a new invoice its number, and counts it as printed once more. Downloads the PDF, showing that saved number, named after the type and number, such as INV_INV-2026-27-0001.pdf . Keeps a copy of the PDF in the app's Saved Invoices folder, in a folder for that client. Uploads it to Google Drive, if you have connected Drive in Settings . Prints it, if auto-print is on in Print Settings or for this client. Saving takes the items out of stock, for rows picked from your products; saving again after changing a quantit"},{"u":"invoices.html#print","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Printing","t":"print\"> On A4, A5 and other sheet sizes , Print opens your browser's print window. On a thermal paper size , it first shows a Print preview of the receipt, with Print , Download PDF and Cancel . See Thermal receipt printing . Printing saves the invoice first, like Save & Download , so what you hand the client is always in your records with the same number."},{"u":"invoices.html#whatsapp","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Sending on WhatsApp","t":"whatsapp\"> WhatsApp opens WhatsApp with the invoice number, date, client, subtotal and total typed in, and your business name. If the client is saved with a phone number, the chat opens with them; otherwise you choose the contact. From the invoice screen the PDF is not attached. Download it with Save & Download and drag it into the chat. The WhatsApp button on the Dashboard can attach the PDF on phones."},{"u":"invoices.html#eway-bill","p":"Making an invoice","s":"E-way bill","t":"eway-bill\"> For tax invoices and delivery challans, E-Way Bill downloads a file, such as EWB-INV-2026-27-0001.json , in the format the NIC e-way bill portal accepts. Upload it there instead of typing everything again. Your own GSTIN must be set in Settings first. An e-way bill is generally needed when goods worth more than ₹50,000 are moved."},{"u":"invoices.html#autosave","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Saving as you go","t":"autosave\"> What you type is kept while the browser tab stays open. If you leave the screen by mistake and come back, the invoice is still there. A new invoice is not stored in your records until you first click Save , Save & Download or Print . Until then the badge says Not saved yet . After that, changes are saved automatically about two seconds after you stop typing."},{"u":"invoices.html#leaving","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Leaving with unsaved changes","t":"leaving\"> If you click Back with unsaved changes, you choose Keep editing , Discard & leave or Save & leave . Closing or reloading the browser tab asks too."},{"u":"invoices.html#keyboard","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Keyboard shortcuts on this screen","t":"keyboard\"> Ctrl + S Save Ctrl + P Save and download the PDF (not print) Ctrl + Enter Add an item row Ctrl + Shift + D Duplicate the last row Enter in the last row Add a row ↑ ↓ Enter Pick from the client or product suggestions Esc Close suggestions or a dialog On a Mac, use ⌘ instead of Ctrl . More shortcuts: Shortcuts, search and notifications ."},{"u":"invoices.html#credit-note","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How to make a credit note","t":"credit-note\"> Start a new invoice Choose Credit Note as the type. Point it at the original In Original Invoice Reference , enter the number of the invoice it corrects. Enter what is being credited Add the returned items, or the price difference, with the same GST rates as the original. Save Its total is subtracted from your sales on the Dashboard, and it goes into GSTR-1 as a credit note."},{"u":"invoices.html#proforma-to-invoice","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Turning a quote into an invoice","t":"proforma-to-invoice\"> When a client accepts a Quotation or a Proforma / Estimate, click Convert to Tax Invoice on it in the Dashboard. A new tax invoice opens with the same client and items, and gets its own number when you save it. The same works for a delivery challan. Once saved, the original shows Converted and its Convert button goes away, so it cannot be turned into a second invoice by mistake."},{"u":"invoices.html#cancel","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Cancelling an invoice","t":"cancel\"> An invoice number, once issued, has to stay in your records, so a saved invoice is cancelled rather than deleted. Cancel it from the Dashboard : it keeps its number, prints with CANCELLED across it, drops out of your totals and GST returns, and its stock goes back. To correct an invoice already sent to a client, the GST way is a credit note rather than a cancellation."},{"u":"invoice-options.html","p":"Customize panel","s":"Customize: what prints and how","t":"The Customize panel on the invoice screen: title, currency, style, colour, every show-or-hide option, paper size and thermal settings, and exactly what each part of the printed invoice shows."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#remembered","p":"Customize panel","s":"Your choices become the default","t":"remembered\"> Open the panel with Customize in the invoice toolbar. Whatever you change here is used for this invoice and remembered for your next new invoice , including the title, reverse charge, TDS and TCS. If a setting was only meant for one invoice, change it back afterwards. A saved invoice keeps the options it was saved with. These are per-invoice settings. The app-wide look, such as fonts, watermarks, copies and translated labels, is in Print and PDF settings . The Customize panel opens inside the Invoice Type card."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#title-currency","p":"Customize panel","s":"Title, currency and exchange rate","t":"title-currency\"> Invoice Title Replaces the printed title, such as TAX INVOICE. Leave it blank to use the type's own title. Thermal receipts ignore it. Currency Rupees to start. See Billing in another currency . Exchange Rate Only for currencies other than rupees. Kept with the invoice."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#recurring","p":"Customize panel","s":"Make this a recurring invoice","t":"recurring\"> Tick 🔁 Make this a recurring invoice to have the app create this invoice again on a schedule, with the same client, items and amounts, a new number and that day's date. Frequency Weekly, Monthly (the default), Quarterly or Yearly Every N 1 to 12. Monthly with 3 means every three months. Next invoice date One month after this invoice, to start End condition Never (until I stop it) , On a specific date , or After N invoices , for example 12 for a one-year monthly contract The schedule is saved when you save the invoice, and can be paused or changed from Recurring ."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#tds-tcs-account","p":"Customize panel","s":"TCS, TDS and the payment account","t":"tds-tcs-account\"> TCS and TDS : see TDS and TCS . Payment account on this invoice : if you have more than one bank account, choose which one prints. New invoices start with your ⭐ default account. The bank details and UPI QR are copied onto the invoice when you save it, so changing the account in Settings later never changes an invoice you have already sent."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#style","p":"Customize panel","s":"PDF style and accent colour","t":"style\"> Style Look Classic Clean, with a coloured bar across the top. The default. Modern A solid colour block behind your business name, with the logo in white. Minimal Simple, with no borders. Boxed grid Every section in ruled boxes: your name large at the top, seller and document details side by side, Billing To and Shipping To, a Work Details line, and an item table filled with empty rows to a fixed height, like a printed quotation pad. Tally style The Tally layout: reference and dispatch boxes beside your details, state names with their codes, taxes inside the item table, amount in words "},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-hide","p":"Customize panel","s":"Showing and hiding parts of the invoice","t":"show-hide\"> Each tick box shows or hides one part of the printed invoice. Hiding something never deletes it. Group Options Off to start Header & branding Logo, business name, address, phone, email, state, Tax ID (GSTIN) Client / Bill-to Client address, phone, email, Place of Supply Invoice meta Invoice number, invoice date, due date Items table HSN/SAC column, Qty column, unit next to the quantity, Rate column, Discount column, Tax % column, GST Cess % column GST Cess Totals Subtotal row, amount in words, round-off line, HSN/SAC tax summary table, tax amount in words The HSN summary and tax in"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#system-generated-note","p":"Customize panel","s":"The \"system-generated invoice\" note","t":"system-generated-note\"> In the Footer group, Note: system-generated invoice adds this line below the terms: Note: This is a system-generated invoice. No signature or stamp is required. It is off unless you turn it on. If you use it, consider turning the signature block off too, so the invoice does not contradict itself."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#paper-size","p":"Customize panel","s":"Paper size","t":"paper-size\"> Option Size A4 Portrait (default) 210 × 297 mm A4 Landscape 297 × 210 mm A5 Portrait (compact) 148 × 210 mm A5 Landscape (2 per A4 sheet) 210 × 148 mm US Letter 216 × 279 mm US Legal 216 × 356 mm B5 176 × 250 mm 80mm Thermal (POS receipt) 72 mm printable 76mm Thermal (kitchen printer) 68 mm printable 58mm Thermal (compact / mobile) 48 mm printable 112mm Thermal (wide receipt) 104 mm printable Custom size Width 30 to 500 mm, height 50 to 1200 mm For a custom size, enter the printer's printable width, not the roll width. Anything under 100 mm wide prints as a receipt. The quick butt"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#thermal-options","p":"Customize panel","s":"Thermal printer settings","t":"thermal-options\"> When a thermal size is chosen, three more settings appear: Font size Small, Medium (the default) or Large Compact mode Tighter item rows. Off to start. Cut mark at bottom Prints a CUT HERE line, for printers without an automatic cutter. On to start. More receipt settings are in Print Settings . See also Thermal receipt printing ."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-header","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the header","t":"printed-header\"> Your side : logo, business name, address with city and PIN, state, GSTIN, email and phone. Each can be hidden. The invoice's side : the title; for a proforma, \"This is not a tax invoice\"; for a credit note, \"Against Invoice\" and the original number; then the number, date and due date; and, for tax invoices and credit notes in India, Reverse Charge Yes or No. With a letterhead set in Print Settings, the header is replaced by your letterhead."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-parties","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: Bill To, Ship To and Place of Supply","t":"printed-parties\"> BILL TO : the client's name, address, state, GSTIN, email and phone. SHIP TO : only when a different delivery address is entered. PLACE OF SUPPLY : the state, with Interstate (IGST) or Intrastate (CGST + SGST) beside it."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-items","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the items table","t":"printed-items\"> Columns, left to right: # , Description (with its longer note underneath), HSN/SAC , Qty with the unit, Rate , Disc. (only when a line has a discount), the tax columns, and Amount . Within your state: CGST and SGST , each with its rate and amount. Another state: one IGST column. Outside India: one column with the local tax name, such as VAT. Amount is the line's value after discount and before tax. The tax is in the columns beside it."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-totals","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the totals","t":"printed-totals\"> On the left, the amount in words and a Scan to pay (UPI) QR code with your UPI ID and the amount. The QR only prints on rupee invoices, with a UPI ID set and a total above zero. On the right, in order: Subtotal, Discount, CGST and SGST or IGST, GST Cess, TCS, Discount on total, Round-off, and Total Due . For a credit note, the last line reads Credit Amount . With TDS, Less: TDS and Net Receivable follow."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-footer","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: notices and footer","t":"printed-footer\"> Reverse charge notice , when turned on. Composition declaration , always on composition bills: \"Composition taxable person, not eligible to collect tax on supplies.\" BANK DETAILS : \"Pay via\" label if on, account name, bank, account number and type, IFSC, SWIFT, and your PAN. EXCHANGE RATE , on foreign-currency invoices. TERMS & CONDITIONS and NOTES , compact or formatted. Signature block : your signature and stamp side by side, \"Authorized Signatory\", and your business name. It only prints when a signature or stamp has been uploaded. Export and SEZ invoices print no LUT declar"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#watermarks","p":"Customize panel","s":"Watermarks","t":"watermarks\"> CANCELLED , in red, on a cancelled invoice. ESTIMATE , very faint, on a proforma. Your own watermark, copy labels such as ORIGINAL and DUPLICATE, REPRINT, page numbers and QR codes come from Print Settings , and only on sheet paper, not receipts."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Thermal receipt printing","t":"Printing bills on a 58 mm or 80 mm receipt printer at a shop counter, from setting it up to what the receipt shows."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#setup","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Setting it up","t":"setup\"> Install the printer in Windows Use the driver that came with it, set the paper size in the driver to your roll width, and make it your default printer, or pick it in the print window each time. Choose the receipt size On an invoice, open Customize and set Paper / print size to 80mm Thermal or 58mm Thermal . The app remembers it for your next invoice. Try a test print In Print Settings , pick the Thermal (80mm) preview tab and click Test Print . Print a real bill Save the invoice, then click Print . A preview of the receipt opens; click Print again. Picking the Retail Shop or Restaurant"},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#print-preview","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"The print preview","t":"print-preview\"> On a receipt size, Print shows the receipt at 160% so you can read it. Its buttons: Print Sends it to the printer. Shows \"Sending…\" while it works. Download PDF Saves and downloads a PDF instead, the same as Save & Download. Cancel Closes it. So does Esc ."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#auto-print","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Printing straight after saving","t":"auto-print\"> At a busy counter, turn on Auto-print on save : Save & Download then prints the receipt as well, with no extra click. It can also be turned on for just one client, in their details."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-contents","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"What a receipt shows","t":"receipt-contents\"> Your logo (if turned on in Print Settings), business name in capitals, tagline, address, GSTIN and phone. The document type, such as TAX INVOICE, then the invoice number, reverse charge, date, and the client's name, GSTIN and phone. Each item: its name, then quantity × rate, GST rate and HSN, with the amount on the right. The amount is quantity × rate, before discount and tax. Subtotal, discount, CGST, SGST or IGST, cess, round-off and TOTAL . Amount in words, bank details, a UPI QR code with \"Scan to pay via UPI\", and notes. Your footer message, such as \"Thank you for your "},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#not-on-receipts","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"What a receipt leaves out","t":"not-on-receipts\"> To fit a narrow roll, receipts do not print: terms and conditions, the signature and stamp, extra pages, the due date, place of supply, client address, TCS, TDS, whole-bill discount lines, the exchange rate, watermarks, the reverse charge and composition notices, or the PDF style and colour. The custom invoice title is not used either. If you need any of these, print that invoice on A4 or A5 instead."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-settings","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Changing how receipts look","t":"receipt-settings\"> Font, boldness, capitals, spacing, darkness, what is shown, the QR size, the footer message, the cut mark and feed lines are all in Print Settings, Thermal receipts ."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-problems","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"When a receipt prints badly","t":"receipt-problems\"> Problem Try Text is cut off on the right Use a smaller printable width: most 80 mm printers print 72 mm, and most 58 mm printers print 48 mm. Use Custom size if yours differs. Print is faint Set Font weight to Bold or Ultra bold, and Thermal ink darkness to Dark. The printer jams or stops half-way Turn on Buffer-safe mode . Blurry text, or nothing prints Set Thermal print method to Via PDF . Paper does not feed far enough to tear Increase Feed lines after cut ."},{"u":"dashboard.html","p":"Dashboard","s":"Dashboard","t":"Your invoices at a glance: what you have sold, what you are owed, what is overdue, and every action you can take on an invoice."},{"u":"dashboard.html#header","p":"Dashboard","s":"At the top","t":"header\"> The count beside the title is every document for the business selected in the sidebar, including estimates, challans and cancelled invoices. New Invoice starts a blank invoice, and CSV import / export brings in or saves many invoices at once (see below ). When a PIN is set, Lock locks the app straight away. The Dashboard with an overdue invoice, the four totals and low stock."},{"u":"dashboard.html#getting-started","p":"Dashboard","s":"The Getting started list","t":"getting-started\"> New installs show four steps. Each ticks itself off once you have really done it, and has a button that takes you there: Step Done when Button Add your business details A business name is saved Open Settings Make your first invoice Any invoice exists Start Add your products or services At least one product is saved Open Add bank details or UPI A bank account or UPI ID is saved Open Settings It disappears when all four are done, or when you close it with ✕ . Read the 5-minute guide opens this documentation in your browser."},{"u":"dashboard.html#support-card","p":"Dashboard","s":"The support card","t":"support-card\"> Once you have made 10 invoices, a small card at the top asks, once a day, whether you would like to support the app, with how much users have given so far. Support with UPI opens Support & About . Not today hides it until tomorrow and Hide for 30 days for a month. It never blocks your work and is never printed on an invoice."},{"u":"dashboard.html#overdue","p":"Dashboard","s":"Overdue invoices and reminders","t":"overdue\"> When any invoice is overdue, a red banner shows how many and how much is outstanding. Click the banner to show only overdue invoices. Remind All lists each overdue invoice with the client, amount and phone number. Remind opens WhatsApp with a polite reminder already written, such as \"Invoice INV/0012 for ₹11,800 was due on 5 Sep 2026. Kindly arrange the payment…\"."},{"u":"dashboard.html#totals","p":"Dashboard","s":"The four totals","t":"totals\"> Total Invoiced The total of your sales, including GST Tax Collected The GST on those sales Outstanding What clients still owe on unpaid and part-paid invoices Invoices How many sales documents there are They cover only the selected business and only real sales. Tax invoices, bills of supply and composition bills count. Credit notes are subtracted. Proforma estimates, delivery challans and cancelled invoices are left out. Foreign-currency sales are shown on their own line, never added to rupees."},{"u":"dashboard.html#low-stock","p":"Dashboard","s":"Low stock","t":"low-stock\"> If alerts are on in Settings , products at or below your threshold scroll past under Low stock , like a news ticker, with Out of Stock in red or the number left in amber. Point at it to stop it; click one to open Products."},{"u":"dashboard.html#invoice-list","p":"Dashboard","s":"Finding an invoice","t":"invoice-list\"> Search By client name or invoice number Financial year All years, or one of the last five Type Any of the six document types Status Unpaid, Partial, Paid, Overdue or Cancelled From / To A range of invoice dates ✕ clears all filters at once."},{"u":"dashboard.html#columns","p":"Dashboard","s":"Choosing the columns","t":"columns\"> Columns lets you show or hide: Date, Invoice #, Type, Client, Amount, Currency, Status, Due date, Print count and Actions. Currency, due date and print count are hidden to start. The Paid column is always shown. Your choice is remembered. A yellow note icon next to a client means the invoice has a private note. Point at it to read it."},{"u":"dashboard.html#status","p":"Dashboard","s":"Status","t":"status\"> Each invoice is Unpaid , Partial , Paid , Overdue or Cancelled . Recording payments sets it for you. Each time the Dashboard opens, unpaid and part-paid invoices past their due date become Overdue, and the row shows how many days late they are. You can also change it from the dropdown on the row. Choosing Paid records a payment for the rest of the balance, so your payment history stays complete. Choosing Unpaid on a paid invoice takes back the payment that marking it Paid recorded, so the Paid column clears and Send reminder comes back. Payments you recorded yourself stay; delete them"},{"u":"dashboard.html#payments","p":"Dashboard","s":"Recording a payment","t":"payments\"> Open it Click the ₹ Payment button on the invoice. The top line shows the total, what is paid, and the balance. Fill it in Enter Amount Received , the Payment Date (today to start), the Payment Mode (Bank Transfer, UPI, Cash, Cheque, Card or Other), and a note such as the transaction ID. Record it Click Record Payment . The status becomes Partial or Paid, and a printable receipt opens. A cancelled invoice cannot take a payment; change its status back first. If the amount is more than the balance, you are asked whether to record it as an overpayment. The extra is kept as the client's"},{"u":"dashboard.html#receipt","p":"Dashboard","s":"The payment receipt","t":"receipt\"> It shows your business details, PAYMENT RECEIPT , the receipt number, date, invoice, payment mode and note, \"Received with thanks from\" the client, the amount (in words for rupees), the invoice total, total paid and balance, and signature lines. Print Receipt prints it on A5."},{"u":"dashboard.html#row-actions","p":"Dashboard","s":"What you can do with an invoice","t":"row-actions\"> The row shows the actions you use most. The rest are in the ⋯ menu at the end of the row; it closes with Esc or a click elsewhere. 👁 View Shows the invoice exactly as it prints, without opening the editor. Print prints it, Esc closes it. The slider at the bottom zooms the preview from 30% to 250% ( − and + step 10%); click the percentage to go back to the normal size. Zoom only changes the preview; the print is always full size. Edit Opens it on the invoice screen. Duplicate A new invoice with the same client and items, a new number and today's date. It starts Unpaid, with no pa"},{"u":"dashboard.html#cancel","p":"Dashboard","s":"Cancelling an invoice","t":"cancel\"> Cancel asks first, then marks the invoice cancelled. It keeps its number, which GST requires, but no longer counts in totals, reports or GST returns, and any stock it used goes back. If you saved or printed its PDF, the copy in the Saved Invoices folder gets CANCELLED across every page. To undo it, click the Undo cancel arrow among the row's actions and answer Yes, undo . It goes back to Unpaid, Partial or Paid, from its payments, the stock is taken out again, and its saved PDF is put back exactly as it was. A cancelled invoice is never shown as overdue."},{"u":"dashboard.html#csv","p":"Dashboard","s":"Importing and exporting invoices as CSV","t":"csv\"> For moving invoices in from Excel, Tally or another program, or out to your CA. Open it Click CSV import / export at the top of the Dashboard. Start from the template Template downloads a CSV with the right columns and an example. Fill it in with Excel or Google Sheets and save it as CSV. Export all as CSV gives what you already have, in the same columns. Choose the file Choose CSV file shows what will happen before anything is saved: how many are ready, which already exist and are skipped, and every row with a problem (a bad date, a missing rate). Rows with problems are not imported; fi"},{"u":"dashboard.html#quick-print","p":"Dashboard","s":"Printing many invoices as one PDF","t":"quick-print\"> The Quick print buttons combine invoices from the list as it is currently filtered into one PDF, one invoice per page: All shown : every invoice in the list Unpaid : only those marked Unpaid, not part-paid or overdue Overdue and Paid For more than five invoices, a message shows how far it has got. For more than 100, you are asked first."},{"u":"dashboard.html#bulk","p":"Dashboard","s":"Ticking several invoices","t":"bulk\"> Tick the box on each row, or the box in the header for every visible row. A bar appears with: Mark paid , Mark unpaid , Mark overdue Change them all, after asking. Mark paid records a payment for each balance. Export JSON Saves the ticked invoices to a file, which can be imported as a backup. Bulk PDF Combines the ticked invoices into one PDF, useful for your CA or for filing. Cancel stops it part-way and keeps what is done. Cancel invoices Cancels the ticked invoices, after asking, and puts their stock back. Marking cancelled invoices as anything else brings them back and takes the sto"},{"u":"clients.html","p":"Clients","s":"Clients","t":"Everyone you bill, what each one owes, their account statement, and how quickly they pay."},{"u":"clients.html#client-list","p":"Clients","s":"The client list","t":"client-list\"> Every client you have saved, and every name you have invoiced, appears as a card, with the ones who owe the most at the top. Search clients… finds them by name. Each card shows the number of invoices, the state and GSTIN, and three figures: Total , Paid , and Outstanding in red, or Overpaid in blue if they have paid too much. Only real sales count: credit notes are subtracted, and quotations, estimates, challans and cancelled invoices are left out. Click a card to open it. Your client list is shared by all your businesses, since the same customer may buy from each."},{"u":"clients.html#client-form","p":"Clients","s":"Adding and editing a client","t":"client-form\"> Add Client opens the form. The same form opens from the invoice screen. Field What to know Client / Business Name Required Address, City, PIN Code The postal label changes with the country Country Starts as your own country. Changing it clears the state. State A list for India, a text box for countries without one GSTIN Checked when you leave the box, as on the invoice: the state is filled in if blank, and typos and a mismatched state are pointed out. See What the GSTIN check tells you . Email, Phone The phone number is used for WhatsApp SEZ unit / Developer India only. Charges I"},{"u":"clients.html#ledger","p":"Clients","s":"A client's account","t":"ledger\"> Open a card to see all their invoices, newest first, with date, number, type, amount and status. Each row has buttons to edit, duplicate, share on WhatsApp, email or delete it. The status can be changed from the row too; choosing Paid records a payment for the balance, as on the Dashboard. At the bottom: Edit Client and Delete Client , or, for a name that was never saved, Save as Client . Deleting a client only removes them from your saved list; their invoices stay. Deleting an invoice here moves it to the Trash for 30 days. It can be restored from Settings, Trash bin . For an invoice"},{"u":"clients.html#ageing","p":"Clients","s":"Ageing: who is slow to pay","t":"ageing\"> When a client owes money, a strip shows it split by how late it is: Current (up to 30 days), 31-60 days , 61-90 days and 90+ days . Lateness is counted from the due date, or from the invoice date when there is none."},{"u":"clients.html#statement","p":"Clients","s":"Statement and ageing PDFs","t":"statement\"> Statement PDF : their whole account, from your business to theirs. It has a summary of invoices, total billed, paid and outstanding, then every invoice, credit note and payment with a running balance marked Dr (they owe you) or Cr (you owe them), and a closing balance. Send it when a bill is disputed. Aging PDF : only what is outstanding, invoice by invoice, with how many days old each is, and totals for each group. Amounts over 60 days are in red. Useful for collection calls."},{"u":"clients.html#import-csv","p":"Clients","s":"Importing clients from a spreadsheet","t":"import-csv\"> Import CSV adds clients from a CSV file, one per row. Save your spreadsheet as CSV first. The first row must name the columns: Column heading Holds name (or client , client name ) Required. Rows without a name are skipped. address , state , gstin , email , phone Optional name,address,state,gstin,email,phone Sharma Traders,12 MG Road,Punjab,03AAAAA0000A1Z5,accounts@sharma.example,9876543210 Clients you already have (same name) are skipped, so importing the same file twice is safe. Other columns, such as city or PIN, are ignored."},{"u":"products.html","p":"Products and stock","s":"Products and stock","t":"Save what you sell once, then pick it on every invoice. Stock goes down as you sell and up as you buy."},{"u":"products.html#product-list","p":"Products and stock","s":"The product list","t":"product-list\"> Products in the sidebar opens your catalogue. The table shows name, HSN/SAC, rate, GST %, unit and stock. Point at a name to see its description. Search by name or HSN. The product list. Low stock shows in amber, none in red."},{"u":"products.html#add-product","p":"Products and stock","s":"Adding a product or service","t":"add-product\"> Field What to know Product / Service Name Required HSN / SAC Code HSN for goods, SAC for services Purchase Price What you pay the supplier. Filled in on new purchase bills. Selling Price What you charge. Filled in on new invoices, and shown as the rate in the list. GST % Type the rate, such as 18 Unit Pcs to start, or any unit from the list, including your own custom units Stock Quantity How many you have now Description For your own reference Deleting a product does not change invoices that used it."},{"u":"products.html#bulk-edit","p":"Products and stock","s":"Changing many products at once","t":"bulk-edit\"> Bulk edit turns the list into a grid you can type in: name, HSN/SAC, purchase price, selling price, GST %, unit and stock. Changed rows are highlighted. Save changes saves them all in one go; Cancel drops them. Search first to edit only some products. A product needs a name, and GST % must be 0 to 100; if a row breaks a rule, nothing is saved and you are told which product to fix. Print / PDF , Excel and CSV above the list save the products shown, with prices, GST and stock."},{"u":"products.html#stock","p":"Products and stock","s":"How stock is counted","t":"stock\"> Selling : saving a Tax Invoice, Bill of Supply, Composition bill or Delivery Challan takes the quantity out, for rows picked from your products. Change the quantity later and save, and only the difference moves. Returns : a Credit Note puts the quantity back. Quotations and proformas move no stock. The invoice you convert them into does. Buying : saving a purchase bill adds the quantity in, and adds any new item to your products. Cancelling an invoice puts its stock back; un-cancelling takes it out again. Out of Stock shows in red at zero or below. Purchases and deletions never take st"},{"u":"products.html#low-stock","p":"Products and stock","s":"Low-stock alerts","t":"low-stock\"> A product at or below your threshold shows its stock in amber here, is listed on the Dashboard, and adds to the notification bell. The threshold is 5 to start; change it, or turn alerts off, in Settings . It is one threshold for every product."},{"u":"products.html#import","p":"Products and stock","s":"Importing products from a spreadsheet","t":"import\"> Import CSV loads a price list. The first row must name the columns: Column heading Holds name (or product , product name ) Required hsn (or hsn code , sac ) HSN or SAC code rate (or price ) Selling price gst% (or tax% , taxpercent , tax ) GST rate, such as 18. Note: no space before the %. unit Nos if left out stock (or quantity ) Opening stock description Optional name,hsn,rate,gst%,unit,stock A4 Paper Ream,4802,280,12,Nos,50 Website Maintenance,998314,5000,18,Month,0 Products you already have (same name) are skipped, so importing the same file twice is safe."},{"u":"purchases.html","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Purchase bills","t":"Record every supplier bill, so the GST you paid comes back as input tax credit and your stock stays right. Includes reading a bill from a photo."},{"u":"purchases.html#purchase-list","p":"Purchase bills","s":"The purchase list","t":"purchase-list\"> At the top, Total Purchases , GST (ITC Eligible) and Entries add up what is shown. Search by supplier, invoice number or GSTIN, and pick a financial year (one of the last five) or All years. The table shows date, supplier, GSTIN, invoice number, taxable value, tax, total, status and actions, with totals at the bottom. Each row has: the eye, to view the bill without downloading anything; the pencil, to edit it; the bin, to delete it. The view has Download PDF ."},{"u":"purchases.html#add-purchase","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Adding a purchase bill","t":"add-purchase\"> Add Purchase opens the form: Field What to know Date Today to start Payment Status Unpaid, Paid or Partial Supplier Name Required. Suppliers you have used before are suggested; picking one fills in their GSTIN, address and whether they are in another state. Supplier GSTIN 15 characters Supplier Address Optional. Printed on the purchase bill PDF. Invoice Number Required. The supplier's invoice number. Note Optional Inter-state purchase See Suppliers in another state Each item row has Name , HSN , Qty , Rate , Tax % (0, 0.1, 0.25, 3, 5, 12, 18 or 28, or Other… for any rate) and Ce"},{"u":"purchases.html#round-off","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Round-off","t":"round-off\"> If the supplier rounded their total to the rupee, tick Apply round-off so yours matches, for example ₹1,234.56 becomes ₹1,235. It is off to start, since most bills already match the line items."},{"u":"purchases.html#interstate","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Suppliers in another state","t":"interstate\"> If the supplier charged IGST because they are in a different state, the bill is Inter-state purchase , and the credit goes to IGST in GSTR-3B rather than CGST and SGST. The box ticks itself when you type the supplier's full GSTIN: its first two digits are their state code, compared with your business's. You can still change it for the rare exception."},{"u":"purchases.html#payment-status","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Paying suppliers","t":"payment-status\"> Change a bill's status straight from the coloured Status dropdown in the list: Unpaid in amber, Paid in green, Partial in purple."},{"u":"purchases.html#stock","p":"Purchase bills","s":"What saving does to your products","t":"stock\"> Each item on the bill is matched to your products by name: A product you already have : its stock goes up by the quantity, and its purchase price is updated. When you edit a bill, only the difference is added, and a row you remove is taken back out. A new item : it is added to your products, with the rate as both purchase and selling price, and the quantity as its stock. Check its selling price afterwards. Deleting a bill takes its quantities back out of stock."},{"u":"purchases.html#ocr","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Reading a bill from a photo","t":"ocr\"> Open it Click Import from image (OCR) . Choose the picture Click or drag a photo or scan of the bill: PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 8 MB. PDFs are not accepted; take a screenshot of the page instead. Read it Click Extract fields . It takes a few seconds, with a percentage showing progress. Check everything The supplier, GSTIN, invoice number, date and grand total are filled in, with the line items it could read: name, HSN, quantity, rate and GST rate. Items that match your saved products take your stored HSN and GST rate. Fix anything wrong, add or remove rows. Use it Use these values opens th"},{"u":"purchases.html#export","p":"Purchase bills","s":"For your accountant","t":"export\"> Print / PDF , Excel and CSV above the list give the purchase register for the current search and year, oldest first, with a total row: date, supplier, GSTIN, invoice number, taxable amount, tax, cess, inter-state, round-off, total, status and note."},{"u":"purchases.html#csv-purchases","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Importing purchase bills from CSV","t":"csv-purchases\"> Open it Click CSV import / export at the top of Purchases. Start from the template Template downloads a CSV with the right columns and an example. Fill it in with Excel or Google Sheets and save it as CSV. Export all as CSV gives what you already have, in the same columns. Choose the file Choose CSV file shows what will happen before anything is saved: how many are ready, which already exist and are skipped, and every row with a problem (a bad date, a missing rate). Rows with problems are not imported; fix the file and choose it again. Import Click Import . A message says how m"},{"u":"purchases.html#unassigned","p":"Purchase bills","s":"\"Not assigned to a business\"","t":"unassigned\"> If you have more than one business, bills saved before you started keeping them separate show under all of them, with a banner. Assign to moves them all to the business now selected. Only do this if they belong to it. The same banner appears on Expenses, Recurring and Receipts."},{"u":"expenses.html","p":"Expenses","s":"Expenses","t":"Costs that are not stock, such as rent, electricity, software or travel, for your profit and loss and for the GST credit on them."},{"u":"expenses.html#expense-list","p":"Expenses","s":"The expense list","t":"expense-list\"> Total Expenses , GST Paid (ITC) and Entries add up what is shown. Search by description, vendor or bill number, and filter by category and financial year. The table shows date, description, category, vendor, amount, GST and payment mode, with totals at the bottom."},{"u":"expenses.html#add-expense","p":"Expenses","s":"Adding an expense","t":"add-expense\"> Field What to know Date Today to start Category See the list below. Other to start. Description Required, such as \"AWS Hosting - March\" Amount (incl. GST) Required. The full amount you paid. GST % (for ITC) The GST rate on the bill. The GST inside the amount is worked out and shown underneath. Vendor Name, Vendor GSTIN Needed to claim the credit Invoice / Bill No Optional Payment Mode Bank Transfer, UPI, Cash, Cheque, Card or Other Inter-state expense Tick when the vendor charged IGST, as with cloud and software firms billing from another state Note Optional"},{"u":"expenses.html#categories","p":"Expenses","s":"Categories","t":"categories\"> Office Rent, Utilities, Internet & Phone, Software & Tools, Travel, Meals & Entertainment, Office Supplies, Salary & Wages, Professional Fees, Insurance, Marketing & Ads, Raw Materials, Shipping & Courier, Repairs & Maintenance, Bank Charges, GST Paid, Asset Purchase, Personal / Drawings, and Other. The Income Tax screen leaves out Personal / Drawings and Asset Purchase when working out business income, since they are not business expenses for tax. The profit and loss report includes every category."},{"u":"expenses.html#gst-credit","p":"Expenses","s":"How the GST credit is used","t":"gst-credit\"> The GST on each expense is added to your input tax credit in GSTR-3B : to IGST if the expense is inter-state, otherwise split between CGST and SGST. Only claim credit you are entitled to: food, personal spending and bills without the vendor's GSTIN usually do not qualify. Check against GSTR-2B."},{"u":"expenses.html#export","p":"Expenses","s":"For your accountant","t":"export\"> The expense statement: Print / PDF , Excel and CSV above the list save the rows shown, oldest first, with a total: date, description, category, amount, GST amount, GST %, vendor, vendor GSTIN, invoice number, payment mode, inter-state and note. Choose the year and a category, or search, first: for example, all Rent for the year."},{"u":"recurring.html","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Recurring invoices","t":"Invoices that repeat on a schedule, such as a monthly retainer, rent or an annual maintenance contract."},{"u":"recurring.html#two-ways","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Two ways to set one up","t":"two-ways\"> From an invoice (recommended): make the first invoice as usual, and under Customize tick Make this a recurring invoice . This keeps everything on the invoice, including taxes, terms and options, and lets you set Every N and an end date or number of invoices. From the Recurring screen : New Template with a client, frequency, next date, when to stop, type and simple item lines."},{"u":"recurring.html#template-form","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"The New Template form","t":"template-form\"> Quick Select Client Fills in the client's name, GSTIN, state and address Client Name Required Client GSTIN Optional Frequency Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly or Yearly Every 1 to 12. Monthly with 3 means every three months. Next Due Date The 1st of next month, to start Stop Never (until I stop it) , On a specific date , or After N invoices Invoice Type Any of the six types Line Items Description, Qty, Rate and GST%. At least one item with a rate is needed."},{"u":"recurring.html#list","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"The template list","t":"list\"> Each template shows the client, how often (such as \"Every 3 months\"), type, amount, next due date and whether it is Active or Paused . Its buttons: ▶ Generate Now, Pause or Activate, Edit, and Delete. Editing keeps everything the form does not show, such as terms and options from the original invoice. Deleting a template stops future invoices; invoices already made stay. When templates are due, a banner lists them, with a button for each to create its invoice now. The recurring template list."},{"u":"recurring.html#automatic","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"How invoices are created automatically","t":"automatic\"> A few seconds after the app starts, and then once a day while it is running, every active template whose date has come creates its invoice, with a fresh number and that day's date. Its next date then moves on by the schedule, and it stops at its end condition. The notification bell tells you how many were created. They appear on the Dashboard, ready to check and send. If the app was closed for a while, one invoice is created each time it catches up, so a missed month is not skipped."},{"u":"recurring.html#generate-now","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Generate Now","t":"generate-now\"> ▶ creates the invoice straight away, even if the template is paused or not yet due, exactly as the automatic run would: same tax, a fresh number, today's date. Its next date moves on by the schedule and it counts towards \"After N invoices\". Once a template has reached its end, it says so instead. Open the new invoice from the Dashboard to check it before sending."},{"u":"receipts.html","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Payment receipts","t":"Receipts for money you have received, whether against an invoice or not, ready to print."},{"u":"receipts.html#receipt-list","p":"Payment receipts","s":"The receipts list","t":"receipt-list\"> Receipts lists every receipt, newest first: date, receipt number, client, the invoice it was against, amount and mode. Search by client or receipt number. Each row can be printed, edited or deleted. Recording a payment on the Dashboard makes its own receipt, which you print from the payment history there."},{"u":"receipts.html#new-receipt","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Making a receipt","t":"new-receipt\"> Start it Click New Receipt . Pick the invoice, if there is one Quick Select, Unpaid Invoices lists up to 50 unpaid sales invoices. Picking one fills in the client, the amount still owed and the invoice number. Fill in the rest Date, Received From (required), Amount (required), Payment Mode , Reference / Transaction No , Against Invoice and a note. Save Save Receipt gives it the next receipt number. When Against Invoice exactly matches one of your invoice numbers, the payment is also recorded on that invoice, and its status becomes Partial or Paid. If it does not match any invoice"},{"u":"receipts.html#numbers","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Receipt numbers","t":"numbers\"> Receipts have their own series, starting RCP, and follow your invoice number format : separator, financial year and digits. If you set a brand prefix, it is used for receipts too. The next number is given when you save, unless you typed your own, which is kept."},{"u":"receipts.html#print","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Printing","t":"print\"> The print button opens the receipt in a new window and your print dialog. It shows your business name, address and GSTIN, PAYMENT RECEIPT , the receipt number, date, who paid, how, the reference and invoice, the amount in figures and words, any note, and lines for Received By and Authorized Signatory . If nothing happens, allow pop-ups for the app in your browser."},{"u":"receipts.html#delete","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Deleting a receipt","t":"delete\"> Deleting a receipt removes only the receipt. A payment it recorded on an invoice stays there; delete that from the invoice's payment history on the Dashboard if it was a mistake."},{"u":"gst-returns.html","p":"GST returns","s":"GST returns","t":"GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B built from the invoices, purchases and expenses you have already entered, checked against GSTR-2B, and ready to upload to the GST portal."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#period","p":"GST returns","s":"Choosing the period","t":"period\"> At the top, pick Monthly , Quarterly (QRMP) or Full Year : Monthly : a month and year. This month to start. Quarterly : Q1 (Apr-Jun), Q2 (Jul-Sep), Q3 (Oct-Dec) or Q4 (Jan-Mar), and a year. The year is the calendar year of those months, so the Jan-Mar 2027 quarter is Q4 with 2027. Full Year : a financial year, such as FY 2026-27. Everything on the screen follows the period and the business selected in the sidebar."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#whats-included","p":"GST returns","s":"What is included","t":"whats-included\"> GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B use tax invoices and credit notes only. Proforma estimates, bills of supply, composition bills and delivery challans are left out. So are cancelled invoices. The Documents issued table lists every kind of document you numbered, as the portal asks. Input tax credit comes from your purchase bills and expenses with GST."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#top-bar","p":"GST returns","s":"Filed status, portal link and warnings","t":"top-bar\"> R1 Filed / R1 Pending and 3B Filed / 3B Pending : green when filed, red when not. Click to switch, if you marked one by mistake. The status is kept in this browser, for each business and period. GST Portal opens gst.gov.in. A red box lists problems to fix first, such as a client GSTIN in the wrong format, your own GSTIN missing, or export invoices that need adding on the portal by hand. If the period has no invoices and no expenses, a banner reminds you to file a NIL return . The strip shows Invoices , Taxable value, Tax and Net Payable for the period."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-1","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1: your sales","t":"gstr-1\"> The GSTR-1 tab lays your sales out in the portal's tables: Table What is in it B2B Sales (4A) Invoices to GST-registered clients, one row each: GSTIN, client, number, date, place of supply code, Inter or Intra, taxable value, CGST, SGST, IGST and total Credit/Debit Notes (9B) Credit notes, to registered clients or marked Unregistered B2C Sales (7) Sales to unregistered buyers, added up the way the portal's Table 7 takes them: one row for each supply type (intra-state or inter-state), place of supply (such as 10-Bihar) and tax rate. Inter-state B2C invoices above ₹1 lakh (₹2.5 lakh for"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-1-files","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1 downloads","t":"gstr-1-files\"> JSON Export The file you upload to the portal: GSTR1_ GSTIN _ MMYYYY .json . See Checks before the file is made . B2B GSTR1_B2B_Invoices.csv B2C GSTR1_B2C_Small.csv , and GSTR1_B2C_Large.csv if there are any HSN GSTR1_HSN_Summary.csv , with the unit code (UQC) for each unit CDNR GSTR1_CDNR.csv for credit notes to registered clients, GSTR1_CDNUR.csv for unregistered Docs GSTR1_Doc_Summary.csv Mark Filed Marks GSTR-1 filed for this period The CSV files are for checking and for your CA. The JSON is what the portal takes."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#json-checks","p":"GST returns","s":"Checks before the file is made","t":"json-checks\"> The portal rejects some mistakes outright, so the app checks for them first. These stop the download until fixed: An invoice number longer than 16 characters, or with anything other than letters, digits, - or / . An item with a GST rate the portal does not accept. The app accepts 0, 0.1, 0.25, 1, 1.5, 3, 5, 6, 7.5, 12, 18, 28 and 40%. These download with a warning: Items with no HSN code. They are left out of the HSN table. HSN codes shorter than 4 digits, or 6 if you ticked turnover above ₹5 crore in Settings . Custom units, which are sent as OTH (others). Your turnover figures "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#upload","p":"GST returns","s":"Uploading GSTR-1 to the portal","t":"upload\"> Download the JSON JSON Export on the GSTR-1 tab, for the right month. Open the return Log in at gst.gov.in, go to Returns Dashboard , pick the period, and open GSTR-1. Upload it Choose Prepare Offline , upload the JSON, and wait for it to be processed. Add what the file cannot hold Exports, in Table 6A. Check and file Compare the portal's summary with the app's totals, then file with DSC or EVC. Mark it filed Back in the app, click Mark Filed ."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-3b","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-3B: tax to pay","t":"gstr-3b\"> Table What it shows 3.1 Outward supplies (a) taxable sales, (b) zero-rated exports with their IGST, (c) nil 3.2 Inter-state to unregistered Your inter-state sales to unregistered buyers, by state 4 Eligible ITC Credit from purchases and expenses, by IGST, CGST and SGST 6 Tax payment Output tax, the credit used against it, and the Net Tax Payable for each tax, plus any credit carried forward Credit is used in the order the law sets: IGST credit first (against IGST, then CGST, then SGST), then CGST credit (against CGST, then IGST) and SGST credit (against SGST, then IGST). CGST credit "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-2b","p":"GST returns","s":"Checking your credit against GSTR-2B","t":"gstr-2b\"> Download GSTR-2B On the portal: Returns , GSTR-2B , Download JSON . Import it On the GSTR-2B Reconciliation tab, click Import 2B JSON and choose the file. Read the results Each entry is matched to your purchase bills by the supplier's GSTIN and invoice number. ✓ Matched In both, and the amounts agree to within ₹1 ⚠ Amount mismatch In both, but the amounts differ ⚠ Books only In your purchases but not in GSTR-2B. The supplier may not have filed yet. ⚠ 2B only In GSTR-2B but not entered in the app Click a count to show only those rows. Export reconciliation CSV saves the result. Chase "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#tds-tcs","p":"GST returns","s":"TDS and TCS report","t":"tds-tcs\"> The TDS / TCS Report tab adds up the period's invoices that have TDS or TCS : TDS Receivable : tax your clients should have deducted, which you claim against your own income tax. By quarter and section. TCS Collected : tax you collected, which must be deposited and reported in Form 27EQ. Export TDS CSV and Export TCS CSV list every invoice with quarter, section, rate, client, GSTIN, PAN, taxable value and amount. They are for your CA to prepare Form 26Q and 27EQ from; they are not the forms themselves."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#filing-guide","p":"GST returns","s":"The Filing Guide tab","t":"filing-guide\"> Step-by-step portal instructions inside the app, with due dates, late fees and interest: Regular Filing : GSTR-1 in 9 steps, then GSTR-3B in 7, with tips. NIL Return : when a NIL return is due, and how to file it, including by SMS. Common Errors & Fixes : portal errors and what to do, and the GST rules worth remembering. Tick each step's circle as you go. The ticks are not saved."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#nil-return","p":"GST returns","s":"NIL returns","t":"nil-return\"> If a period has no sales and no expenses, the app says so. A NIL return is still due, on time. The Filing Guide's NIL Return tab shows how, including by SMS to 14409."},{"u":"reports.html","p":"Reports","s":"Reports","t":"Profit and loss, who owes you and for how long, party outstanding by month, your best clients, your best-selling products, and closing stock with its value. Every report prints and downloads as Excel or CSV."},{"u":"reports.html#included","p":"Reports","s":"What the reports include","t":"included\"> The sales tabs cover the business selected in the sidebar and count only real sales, as the Dashboard does: tax invoices, bills of supply and composition bills count; credit notes are subtracted; proforma estimates, delivery challans and cancelled invoices are left out. Purchase bills are not part of these reports; they are in Income Tax, ITR Summary ."},{"u":"reports.html#export","p":"Reports","s":"Printing and downloading a report","t":"export\"> Every report table has three buttons: Print / PDF Opens the table alone on its own page. Choose your printer, or Save as PDF . Excel Downloads an .xlsx file. Amounts are numbers, so Excel can total and sort them. CSV The same table as CSV, for any spreadsheet or your CA's software. They export what the screen shows: the period, currency and filters you chose. The Expense statement and Purchase register have the same buttons on their own screens."},{"u":"reports.html#profit-loss","p":"Reports","s":"Profit & Loss","t":"profit-loss\"> Choose Fiscal Year or Month / Year . If you bill in more than one currency, a Currency choice appears, since different currencies are never added together. Revenue (ex. tax) Sales without GST Expenses (ex. GST) Expenses without their GST Net Profit or Net Loss The difference. Green for profit, red for loss. Margin Profit as a percentage of revenue The Profit & Loss Statement sets it out: total revenue, less GST collected; total expenses, less GST on expenses; and the result. The Monthly Breakdown shows revenue, expenses and profit or loss for each month with activity. The same pe"},{"u":"reports.html#outstanding","p":"Reports","s":"Outstanding & Aging","t":"outstanding\"> Every unpaid or part-paid invoice, whatever its date, grouped by how late it is: Current (0-30 days) , 31-60 , 61-90 and 90+ days , counted from the due date. The table lists client, invoice, date, due date, amount, paid, outstanding and days overdue, latest first, with the worst in red. Filter by client name… narrows the table and the totals together."},{"u":"reports.html#party-outstanding","p":"Reports","s":"Party Outstanding","t":"party-outstanding\"> The same money owed, laid out the way Tally does it: one row per party, one column per month, a Total for each party on the right and for each month at the bottom. Each unpaid amount sits in the month of its invoice. Choose Financial year (Apr-Mar) , the default, or Calendar year (Jan-Dec) , and the year. Bills from before that year that are still unpaid appear in an Earlier column, so nothing owed drops out of the total. Print / PDF opens the table on its own page, landscape; choose your printer or Save as PDF. Excel and CSV download it. Only sales count; estimates, challa"},{"u":"reports.html#clients","p":"Reports","s":"Client Analytics","t":"clients\"> Top clients by revenue : the ten who bought the most, with invoice counts. Highest outstanding : the ten who owe the most, and what share of their billing is unpaid. All clients breakdown : invoices, revenue, paid, outstanding and last invoice date for everyone. Revenue here includes GST."},{"u":"reports.html#products","p":"Reports","s":"Product Performance","t":"products\"> Top revenue producers : the ten items that brought in the most. Most units sold : the ten sold in the largest quantity. All products : HSN, quantity sold, revenue, average rate, number of sales and when last sold. Revenue here is after line discounts and without tax. Credit notes are subtracted. Delivery charges are not a product and are left out."},{"u":"reports.html#stock","p":"Reports","s":"Stock","t":"stock\"> Closing stock of every product at the end of a month, and what it is worth. Choose the month; the current month shows today's stock. Closing qty is worked back from today's stock, using the dates of your invoices and purchase bills. Rate is the purchase price. A product with no purchase price is valued at its selling price, marked with *. Value is quantity × rate, with the Total stock value at the bottom. Negative stock shows in red and is not added in. Stock you typed in by hand on the Products screen has no date, so it counts as if it changed today. Products are shared by all your bu"},{"u":"income-tax.html","p":"Income tax","s":"Income tax helper","t":"Estimate your income tax under the old and new regimes, presumptive taxation, advance tax, bank statement import, and an ITR-4 summary to file from."},{"u":"income-tax.html#tabs","p":"Income tax","s":"The five tabs","t":"tabs\"> Regime Calculator Old and new regimes side by side, and which costs less Presumptive Income under sections 44AD, 44ADA and 44AE Advance Tax Instalments, and interest for paying late Bank Statement Import Read a bank CSV and sort each transaction ITR Summary The year in one place, and the ITR-4 summary PDF What you type on the first three tabs is remembered in this browser."},{"u":"income-tax.html#regime-calculator","p":"Income tax","s":"Regime Calculator","t":"regime-calculator\"> First tell it your age (under 60, 60 to 79, or 80 or older), whether your parents are 60 or older , and whether you are a government employee . These decide the old-regime slabs and the limits for 80D, 80DDB and 80CCD(2). Then enter your income, in rupees, for the year: Gross Salary , as in box 1 of Form 16. The standard deduction is applied for you. Business / Professional Income : filled in from your rupee sales, less purchases and business expenses, all without GST, if you leave it at zero. Change it if your books say otherwise. House Property (rent less municipal tax an"},{"u":"income-tax.html#presumptive","p":"Income tax","s":"Presumptive income","t":"presumptive\"> Choose the section that fits you: 44AD Trading, retail and manufacturing. Enter digital and cash turnover: 6% of digital and 8% of cash counts as income. The limit is ₹3 crore if cash is no more than 5% of turnover, otherwise ₹2 crore. 44ADA Professionals such as CAs, doctors, lawyers and consultants. 50% of receipts counts as income, up to ₹75 lakh of receipts (₹50 lakh if cash is over 5%). 44AE Owners of up to 10 goods vehicles. ₹1,000 per tonne per month for heavy vehicles, ₹7,500 per month for others. If your real profit is higher, enter it: you cannot declare less than the p"},{"u":"income-tax.html#advance-tax","p":"Income tax","s":"Advance tax","t":"advance-tax\"> Based on the recommended regime's tax, less TDS already deducted . If what is left is under ₹10,000, no advance tax is due. Otherwise the schedule shows how much is due by 15 June (15%), 15 September (45%), 15 December (75%) and 15 March (100%). Tick Presumptive to pay it all by 15 March instead. Add the payments you made with + Add payment , and the interest for paying late or short, under sections 234B and 234C, is worked out."},{"u":"income-tax.html#bank-import","p":"Income tax","s":"Bank statement import","t":"bank-import\"> Download a CSV From net-banking or your bank's app, save the statement for the year as CSV. Excel files must be saved as CSV first; PDFs are not accepted. Drop it in SBI, HDFC, ICICI, Axis, Kotak, PNB and Yes Bank formats are recognised, and most others work too. It is read on your computer; nothing is uploaded. Check the categories Each transaction is sorted by its description, such as salary, interest, rent received, investments, insurance, GST or business expense. Change any that are wrong. Mark your sales receipts as Business receipts yourself. Push to the calculator Push to "},{"u":"income-tax.html#itr-summary","p":"Income tax","s":"ITR Summary and the ITR-4 PDF","t":"itr-summary\"> The year's figures from the app: sales, trading purchases and business expenses (all without GST, and without drawings and asset purchases) and net business income, then salary, rent, other income and capital gains from the calculator, and the tax under each regime. Download ITR-4 Summary makes a PDF with each ITR-4 (Sugam) field worked out, from income to deductions to tax and advance tax, to copy into incometax.gov.in or hand to your CA. ITR-4 is only for some taxpayers: if you have capital gains, or income above the limits, you need a different form."},{"u":"settings.html","p":"Settings","s":"Settings","t":"Every section of Settings, in the order it appears: your business, bank accounts, invoice numbers, logo and stamp, more than one business, terms, features, stock alerts, region, app lock, backups, Google Drive, import and export, and updates."},{"u":"settings.html#save-bar","p":"Settings","s":"Saving your changes","t":"save-bar\"> The section buttons stay at the top of Settings as you scroll: each jumps straight to its section, and the one you are reading is highlighted. At the bottom, one bar saves the whole page. It shows ✓ All changes saved , or, in amber, which sections have unsaved changes, with Discard to undo them all and Save all changes to save them all in one click. Not everything waits for a Save. Save all changes covers every section in the last two columns: Saves by itself as you change it Has its own Save button Needs Save Profile Payment accounts, Modules, Region, App lock Invoice number format"},{"u":"settings.html#company-details","p":"Settings","s":"Company details","t":"company-details\"> The header of every invoice. Field What to know Business Name Required Country India to start. The list follows your Region . Address, City, PIN Code State The one to get right: it decides whether GST is split into CGST and SGST or charged as IGST GSTIN Warns if the format looks wrong. The label changes for other countries, such as VAT or TRN. Email, Phone"},{"u":"settings.html#gstr-details","p":"Settings","s":"GSTR filing details","t":"gstr-details\"> Indian businesses only, and only used in the GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B files . All optional. Aggregate turnover (AATO) is above ₹5 crore : tick it if so. HSN codes then need 6 digits instead of 4. Previous FY aggregate turnover and Current FY turnover so far , in rupees. You can also change these on the portal while filing."},{"u":"settings.html#payment-accounts","p":"Settings","s":"Bank accounts and UPI","t":"payment-accounts\"> Add as many bank and UPI accounts as you like with + Add account . Each account has: Field What to know Label Your name for it, such as \"HDFC Current - 1234\" Account Holder Name Leave blank to use your business name Bank Name, Account Number Account Type Optional: Savings, Current, Cash Credit, Overdraft, NRE or NRO IFSC Code Or the local bank code outside India SWIFT / BIC Optional, for payments from abroad UPI ID Optional. With one, rupee invoices using this account carry a QR code the client can scan to pay the exact amount. Internal notes Never printed Set as default The"},{"u":"settings.html#invoice-numbers","p":"Settings","s":"Invoice number format","t":"invoice-numbers\"> The preview at the top shows exactly how the next number will look. Branded Sequential PREFIX/2026-27/0001 , with the financial year. The default. Simple Sequential PREFIX/0001 Random PREFIX/A3X9K2 Start numbering from lets tax invoices carry on from your paper bill book: enter 1001 and the next tax invoice is .../1001 , then 1002 and so on. When you save, the app shows the new next number and asks you to confirm, because numbers never go back down. If you have already gone past it, numbering simply continues; a number already used is never given again. Quotations, challans, "},{"u":"settings.html#branding","p":"Settings","s":"Logo, signature and stamp","t":"branding\"> Upload each one separately. Any image up to 5 MB works; large images are made smaller for you. A signature or stamp on a transparent PNG looks best. Each has a size slider: logo 24 to 80 pixels high, signature 30 to 110, stamp 30 to 120. Click Save Profile to keep them. The signature and stamp print side by side above the signatory's name, and on a long invoice they always move to the next page together rather than being split. A photo from an iPhone in HEIC format may not open; share it as JPEG first."},{"u":"settings.html#multiple-businesses","p":"Settings","s":"More than one business","t":"multiple-businesses\"> If you run more than one business, each gets its own profile with its own GSTIN, bank accounts, logo and signature, and its own books . Invoices, totals, purchases, expenses, receipts, recurring invoices, reports and GST returns all follow the business selected at the top of the sidebar. + Add New Profile saves the business on screen to the list, then clears the form for the new one. Fill it in and click Save Profile. Save as Profile saves the form into the list, or updates the entry with the same name. Switch on a card changes business. The current one is saved first. De"},{"u":"settings.html#terms","p":"Settings","s":"Terms and conditions templates","t":"terms\"> Keep the terms you use as templates, then pick one on each invoice. Quick Start : one click adds a ready-made set for Services, Goods, Manufacturing and Trading, Export, or Freelancer. + New Template : give it a name and paste your terms. Deleting a template does not change invoices that used it."},{"u":"settings.html#print-settings","p":"Settings","s":"Print and PDF settings","t":"print-settings\"> The app-wide look of every invoice has its own page: Print and PDF settings ."},{"u":"settings.html#modules","p":"Settings","s":"Turning features off","t":"modules\"> Untick anything you do not use, and it disappears from the sidebar and forms. Your data is kept, and ticking it again brings it all back. Group Features Sales & Invoicing Invoices (always on), Recurring invoices, Payment receipts Directory Clients (always on), Products & Services Purchases & Expenses Expense tracker, Purchase bills, GSTR-2B reconciliation GST & Tax (India) GSTR-1 / GSTR-3B, E-Way Bill, TDS / TCS on invoices ( off to start), Income Tax Helper Reports Dashboard (always on), Reports Integrations Google Drive backup, UPI QR code on invoices 🇮🇳 marks features that only "},{"u":"settings.html#stock","p":"Settings","s":"Low-stock alerts","t":"stock\"> Show low-stock alerts is on to start. Set the threshold with a chip, 0, 3, 5 (recommended) or 10, or type a number, then click Save . With alerts off, stock is still counted; you are just not warned."},{"u":"settings.html#region","p":"Settings","s":"Region","t":"region\"> 🇮🇳 India only GST, rupees first, GSTR-1 and 3B, e-way bill, UPI QR 🌍 International VAT and other tax names, several currencies, no India-only features 🌐 Both / Auto All countries, chosen per invoice. The default. It saves as soon as you click, and changes the country lists and which features you see. Your data is not touched. Region, Print settings and your other display choices are also kept in the app's data folder, so they come back even if the browser clears its saved data."},{"u":"settings.html#lock","p":"Settings","s":"App lock (PIN)","t":"lock\"> For a computer other people also use. Turn on PIN lock , choose 6 or 8 digits, type the PIN twice and click Save PIN . From then on the app asks for it each time it is opened. It is off to start. Lock now locks the app straight away, when you step away. So do Lock on the Dashboard, Lock app in the sidebar and Ctrl + Shift + L anywhere. Anything you were typing is still there after you unlock. Change PIN and Turn off need the current PIN. After five wrong tries in a row, wait 30 seconds before the next. It locks the screen only; it does not encrypt your files. Keep your backups safe as b"},{"u":"settings.html#backups","p":"Settings","s":"Daily backups and the trash bin","t":"backups\"> Settings lists the automatic daily backups, with Backup now , Restore and Delete , and the trash bin for deleted invoices. See Automatic daily backups and Trash ."},{"u":"settings.html#google-drive","p":"Settings","s":"Google Drive","t":"google-drive\"> The easy way : install Google Drive for Desktop , sign in, and move the app's Saved Invoices folder into your Drive, or set it to sync. Every PDF you download is then in your Drive, on any device. No setup in the app is needed. Direct upload , under Advanced , is for people comfortable with Google Cloud: it needs a Google OAuth Client ID of your own. Enter it and a folder name, click Save Profile, then Connect Google Drive . After that, Save & Download uploads each invoice PDF, and a backup can be saved to Drive when exporting."},{"u":"settings.html#data","p":"Settings","s":"Import and export (Data Management)","t":"data\"> Export Backup… and Import Backup… move your data in and out as one file. See Export everything to one file ."},{"u":"settings.html#updates","p":"Settings","s":"Updates","t":"updates\"> Check for Updates shows your version and the latest. If there is a newer one, Update Now backs up your data and installs it; reload the page when it finishes. See Updating ."},{"u":"backup.html","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Backups, updates and moving PC","t":"Your data is plain files on your own computer. Here is how it is backed up, how to keep a copy somewhere safe, update the app, and move to a new computer."},{"u":"backup.html#where-data-lives","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Where your data is","t":"where-data-lives\"> Everything is in the _system\\data folder inside the app's folder. The installer hides _system to keep things tidy; in File Explorer, turn on View, Show, Hidden items to see it. Open Data Folder in the Control Panel opens it for you. Downloaded PDFs are also kept in the app's Saved Invoices folder, one folder per client."},{"u":"backup.html#automatic-backups","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Automatic daily backups","t":"automatic-backups\"> Every day the app copies all your data into a dated backup, and keeps the last 30 days. They are listed in Settings, Backup Management : Backup now makes one straight away. Restore puts all your data back as it was on that day. It saves what you have now first, so you can go back if it looks wrong. Reload the page afterwards. Delete removes one backup to free space. These are on the same computer Daily backups protect you from mistakes, not from a broken hard disk or a lost laptop. Keep a copy somewhere else too."},{"u":"backup.html#backup-copy","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Keeping a copy somewhere else","t":"backup-copy\"> Every day, automatically, on another drive. In Settings, Backup Management , type a folder such as D:\\FreeGSTBill (another drive, a USB disk or a synced folder) under Also keep a copy of every daily backup in this folder , and click Save folder . The app checks it can write there, then copies each daily backup into FreeGSTBill Backups\\ date inside it, keeping 30 days. If a copy fails (a USB disk not plugged in), Settings says so. Stop copying turns it off. If the computer fails: install the app again, set the same folder, and its backups appear in the list with Restore . Or by ha"},{"u":"backup.html#export-import","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Export everything to one file","t":"export-import\"> In Settings, Data Management , Export Backup… lets you tick what to include; everything is ticked to start: active business profile, all business profiles, invoices, clients, products, expenses, purchase bills, recurring invoices, receipts, terms templates, app settings, and local preferences such as custom units and theme. Download Backup saves freegstbill-backup- date .json . Tick Also save a copy to my Google Drive if you have connected Drive. Import Backup… reads a backup file and shows what is in it, with a count for each part, before anything changes. Tick the parts to re"},{"u":"backup.html#trash","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Trash","t":"trash\"> Invoices deleted from a client's account on the Clients screen go to the trash for 30 days. In Settings, Backup Management , Restore brings one back, and Delete forever removes it and its PDF for good."},{"u":"backup.html#move-pc","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Moving to a new computer","t":"move-pc\"> On the old computer Click Export for Move in the Control Panel , or Move to another PC in the launcher under More options . It saves your data and settings as one ZIP on your Desktop. Copy it to a pen drive or cloud storage. On the new computer Install the app as usual. Bring your data in In the new Control Panel, click Choose Backup ZIP under Restore Backup and pick the file. You can use an exported backup file instead: export on the old computer, and import it in Settings on the new one. One computer at a time Do not run the same data on two computers at once, for example through a"},{"u":"backup.html#update","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Updating","t":"update\"> Any of these installs the newest version: The Update to v… button that appears in the sidebar when a new version is out. It shows what changed, with Update Now , Remind me later and Skip this version . Update Now in Settings, App Updates . Update Now in the Control Panel . In the launcher, More options , then Update to the latest version . Every update first saves a backup of your data in Documents\\FreeGSTBill Backups , then replaces the app. It never touches your data folder or your saved PDFs. It takes about a minute; reload the page when it finishes. To update by hand instead: down"},{"u":"control-panel.html","p":"Control Panel","s":"Control Panel","t":"Update, back up, restore, move to another PC, open your folders, and stop the app, from inside the app."},{"u":"control-panel.html#about","p":"Control Panel","s":"What it is","t":"about\"> Control Panel in the sidebar does the launcher's jobs without leaving the app. At the top it shows your system, Node.js version, the port the app runs on, and how much space your data takes."},{"u":"control-panel.html#actions","p":"Control Panel","s":"The buttons","t":"actions\"> Card Button What it does Update Software Update Now Downloads the latest version. Your data is backed up first and never touched. Backup Data Create Backup Saves your data as a dated ZIP in Documents\\FreeGSTBill Backups . Restore Backup Choose Backup ZIP Pick a backup ZIP to restore. What you have now is saved first, as a safety net. Move to Another PC Export for Move Saves your data and settings as one ZIP on your Desktop. See Moving to a new computer . Open Data Folder Open Opens the folder with your bills, clients, products and settings. Open Backups Folder Open Opens Documents\\Fr"},{"u":"control-panel.html#scripts-missing","p":"Control Panel","s":"\"Update and backup scripts not found\"","t":"scripts-missing\"> The Control Panel runs scripts that come with the downloaded ZIP, in the _system folder. This message appears when they are missing, for example when the app was started from source code or copied without them. Install from the downloaded ZIP to get them, or use Export Backup in Settings for your data. Versions 1.10.44 to 1.10.71 showed this message, then called \"Launcher scripts not detected\", on every installed copy by mistake. Update to 1.10.72 or later using the launcher's Update to the latest version . On Linux and macOS only Update and Backup have scripts, so Restore, M"},{"u":"print-settings.html","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print and PDF settings","t":"The app-wide defaults for how every invoice looks on paper and in a PDF: business-type presets, designs, thermal receipts, copies, watermarks, fonts, colours, languages and formats. Each invoice can still override the basics from its own Customize panel."},{"u":"print-settings.html#how-it-saves","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"How these settings save","t":"how-it-saves\"> Open Settings and go to the Print & PDF section. There is no Save button: every change is kept the moment you make it, and the Live preview on the right updates as you type. The preview uses a sample invoice with your business name, so you can see the effect without touching a real invoice. Three buttons sit at the top: Run setup wizard Shows the first-run wizard again the next time the app is reloaded. Reset defaults Puts every print setting back to how it was on a fresh install, straight away and without asking. That includes your saved templates, number prefixes, signature im"},{"u":"print-settings.html#business-type","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Business type","t":"business-type\"> Picking the kind of business you run sets 15 or so settings in one go, and hides options that do not apply to you. You are asked to confirm first, and every setting stays editable afterwards. Business type Set up for Main settings it applies Retail Shop / Kirana A counter with a thermal printer Bold capitals, prints straight after saving, \"Qty × Rate\" lines, no HSN, \"Thank you! Visit again!\", cut mark and 2 feed lines Freelancer / Consultant Professional A4 PDFs Minimalist design, HSN, amount in words, page numbers and header on long invoices Restaurant / Cafe / Bar 80 mm recei"},{"u":"print-settings.html#visual-style","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Visual style","t":"visual-style\"> Eight ready-made designs set the colours and type for both PDFs and thermal receipts in one click. Each card shows a small preview in its own colours; the one in use is marked ACTIVE . Design Suits Look Aurora Freelancers, tech Cool slate with electric blue Editorial Law, consulting Charcoal on warm ivory, capitals Executive Enterprise, B2B Deep navy with soft champagne Whisper Designers, studios Off-white, one hairline, nothing else Sunset Retail, cafes, salons Warm terracotta on cream, with a tagline Monoline Developers, agencies Monospace, dense rows, 90% size Nordic SaaS, st"},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Thermal receipts","t":"thermal\"> These four groups only affect 58 mm and 80 mm receipt printers. They are hidden when your business type prints A4 or A5 PDFs. Typography Setting Options Default Font family Monospace (Courier), or sans-serif Monospace Font size Small, Medium, Large, Extra Large Medium Font weight Normal, Bold, Ultra bold. Thermal heads print bold much darker, so bold is recommended. Bold ALL CAPS mode Every line in capitals, like big supermarket receipts Off Layout Line spacing Compact (saves paper), Normal, Comfortable Normal Header alignment Centre, or left Centre Thermal ink darkness Standard, Dar"},{"u":"print-settings.html#auto-print","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Auto-print on save","t":"auto-print\"> With this on, Save & Download also sends the invoice straight to your default printer, with no extra click. Made for shop counters. Off by default."},{"u":"print-settings.html#watermark","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Watermark","t":"watermark\"> A large, faint diagonal word across every page of the PDF. Turn on Show watermark , then choose either a ready-made word (PAID, DUPLICATE, DRAFT, OVERDUE, COPY, ORIGINAL, CANCELLED or REPRINT; DUPLICATE is selected by default) or your own text. Opacity ranges from very faint (5%) to very strong (40%); medium (15%) is the default. If you choose your own text and leave the box empty, no watermark prints. Watermarks are never printed on thermal receipts. Cancelled invoices get their own CANCELLED mark whatever this setting says."},{"u":"print-settings.html#copies","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Multiple copies (GST rule 48)","t":"copies\"> GST rules expect three copies of an invoice for goods (for the buyer, the transporter and yourself) and two for services. Turn on Print multiple copies with labels and choose 2 or 3 (3 is the default). The PDF then holds every page once for each copy, labelled in a small box at the top right: ORIGINAL FOR RECIPIENT DUPLICATE FOR TRANSPORTER TRIPLICATE FOR SUPPLIER"},{"u":"print-settings.html#multi-page","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Invoices longer than one page","t":"multi-page\"> Page numbers Prints \"Page 2 of 3\" at the bottom right of the second page onwards. The first page is not numbered. On Business name header on pages 2+ Repeats your business name, with a line under it, at the top of every page after the first On Both only appear when an invoice runs to more than one page. Page breaks always fall between rows, and never through the signature, stamp or an image."},{"u":"print-settings.html#margins","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print margins","t":"margins\"> Top, bottom, left and right, in millimetres, from 0 to 100 (all 0 to start). Use them for pre-printed letterhead, to move the invoice clear of a printed logo, or to leave room for binding."},{"u":"print-settings.html#verification-codes","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Invoice QR and number","t":"verification-codes\"> Invoice number as QR : an 18 mm QR code at the bottom right of the last page, captioned \"Verify invoice\". It holds the invoice number, or, if you give a verification URL such as https://mycompany.com/verify/{invoice_number} , that address with the number filled in. Invoice number as barcode text : prints the invoice number large, in a typewriter font, at the bottom left of the last page, for filing. It is text, not a scannable barcode."},{"u":"print-settings.html#feedback-qr","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Feedback QR","t":"feedback-qr\"> A QR code at the bottom left of the PDF that opens any web address you give it, such as your Google review page or a WhatsApp chat. It only prints once an address is entered. Its caption, \"Rate us · Give feedback\" unless you change it, prints under the code."},{"u":"print-settings.html#signature","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Default signature","t":"signature\"> A signature image (PNG, JPG, WebP or SVG, up to 2 MB) and signatory name used when a business has none of its own. With the name left blank, the business name is used. A signature and stamp uploaded in Settings for a business take priority."},{"u":"print-settings.html#terms-page","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Terms on a separate page","t":"terms-page\"> Print T&C on a separate page moves long terms and notes to a page of their own, instead of squeezing them under the totals. Off by default."},{"u":"print-settings.html#pdf-font","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF font, size and darkness","t":"pdf-font\"> PDF font Helvetica (clean, the default), Times New Roman (formal), or Courier (typewriter style). Thermal receipts have their own font setting. Overall size A slider from 80% to 140%. Smaller fits more on a page; larger is easier to read. The on-screen preview always shows 100%; download a PDF to see the result. Force darker text Darkens grey labels and addresses so they do not fade on paper. On by default. Compact upper header Tightens the space above the items table so more fits on the first page. Off by default. Row density Compact, Normal or Comfortable spacing in tables and sec"},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-compatibility","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Thermal printer compatibility","t":"thermal-compatibility\"> Buffer-safe mode : for cheap or old receipt printers that jam on large print jobs. Prints in black and white at lower quality. Off by default. Thermal print method : Direct , the default, sends sharp text straight to the printer. If your printer or browser mishandles it, choose Via PDF ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#prefixes","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Number prefix for each document type","t":"prefixes\"> Each document type numbers separately, with a built-in prefix: INV for tax invoices, EST for estimates, BOS for bills of supply, COMP for composition, CN for credit notes and DC for delivery challans. Type your own to replace one: letters, numbers, hyphens and underscores only, up to 8 characters. A new prefix starts its own count."},{"u":"print-settings.html#reprint","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Reprint badge","t":"reprint\"> Once an invoice has been printed before, this prints a red \"REPRINT · Copy #2\" (and so on) at the top right of each page, so a copy cannot pass as the original. Off by default. The app counts every print either way."},{"u":"print-settings.html#dual-currency","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Second currency","t":"dual-currency\"> For rupee invoices to clients abroad, shows the total in a second currency too: US dollars, euros, pounds, dirhams, Singapore or Australian dollars, or yen. You set the rate (83 rupees to the dollar to start); there is no live exchange rate. It can go on its own line or in brackets after the rupee amount."},{"u":"print-settings.html#letterhead","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Letterhead","t":"letterhead\"> Upload your printed letterhead as a picture (PNG, JPG or WebP, A4, up to 3 MB) and invoices print on top of it. Hide invoice header block , on by default, drops the app's own header so your details are not printed twice. The switch does nothing until an image is uploaded."},{"u":"print-settings.html#template","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF layout template","t":"template\"> Modern (a coloured header, the default), Classic (conservative), Minimal (lots of white space), Corporate, Minimalist, Boxed grid and Tally style. Corporate and Minimalist are variations of Classic and Minimal. A design chosen under Visual style sets this for you."},{"u":"print-settings.html#colours","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Your own colours","t":"colours\"> Turn on Use custom colours to set six colours with a picker or a hex code. Reset colours to defaults undoes them. Primary text Client name, item names, totals Muted text Labels, addresses, dates and numbers Accent colour Section titles and the table header Accent text Text on the accent colour, usually white Header background Behind the business name and invoice title Divider lines Lines between sections and table rows"},{"u":"print-settings.html#labels-language","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Section labels and language","t":"labels-language\"> Print the section labels in English, Hindi, Tamil, Marathi or Bengali. You can also type your own wording for six labels: BILL TO, PLACE OF SUPPLY, BANK DETAILS, AMOUNT IN WORDS, TERMS & CONDITIONS and NOTES. Your own wording wins over the language."},{"u":"print-settings.html#formats","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Dates, numbers and currency","t":"formats\"> Date format 02 Apr 2026 (the default), 02-Apr-2026, 02/04/2026, 04/02/2026 (US), 2026-04-02, or ISO 8601 Number grouping 1,00,000.00 (Indian, the default), 100,000.00 (Western), 100.000,00 (European) Decimal places 0, 2 (the default), 3 or 4 Currency symbol Before the number (₹100, the default) or after it"},{"u":"print-settings.html#round-off","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Round off invoice totals","t":"round-off\"> Under Totals . When on, new invoices round the grand total to the nearest rupee and print the difference as a Round-off line. It is on for new installs. You can still turn it off for one invoice in Customize , under Totals. Changing it never alters invoices you have already saved."},{"u":"print-settings.html#tax-rates","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Extra GST rates","t":"tax-rates\"> The built-in rates are 0, 5, 12, 18 and 28%. Add your own, such as 3% for jewellery or 0.25% for diamonds, as numbers separated by commas, and they appear in the rate list on every invoice."},{"u":"print-settings.html#templates","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Saved templates","t":"templates\"> Save your whole print setup under a name, such as \"Retail v1\", with Save current as template . Load brings one back after asking, and replaces your current settings, so save the current setup first if you want to keep it."},{"u":"print-settings.html#preview","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"The live preview","t":"preview\"> Three tabs: PDF (A4) , Thermal (80mm) , and Split view with both side by side. It shows a sample invoice to TEST/PRINT/0001 with three items, using your business name, so terms and notes are not shown."},{"u":"shortcuts.html","p":"Getting around","s":"Getting around the app","t":"The sidebar, switching business, notifications, quick search with Ctrl + K, keyboard shortcuts and dark mode."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#sidebar","p":"Getting around","s":"The sidebar","t":"sidebar\"> From top to bottom: Your business , with a pencil to edit it. If you have more than one, click the name to switch . The screens : Dashboard, New Invoice, Clients, Products, Expenses, Purchases, Recurring, Receipts, Reports, GST Returns, Income Tax, and User Guide , which opens this documentation in your browser (it needs internet). Features you turn off disappear from here. Update to v… , when a new version is out. Notifications , Dark Mode or Light Mode , Support & About , Control Panel and Settings . At the bottom, App Ready when all is well. At the end of the Dashboard, below the "},{"u":"shortcuts.html#support","p":"Getting around","s":"Support & About","t":"support\"> Who makes the app, and how to help it grow. Free ways come first: star it on GitHub, tell another business, report a bug or ask for a feature. If you want to give money, scan the UPI QR with any UPI app, for any amount. The page also lists what OM RAJ builds for businesses: custom software and web apps, changes to this app, setup and data migration, support plans, AI integration and automation, and mobile apps. The app stays free whatever you choose. Nothing is locked, and nothing is ever printed on your invoices. Once you have made 10 invoices, the Dashboard shows a small support ca"},{"u":"shortcuts.html#switch-business","p":"Getting around","s":"Switching business","t":"switch-business\"> With more than one business saved, click its name at the top of the sidebar and choose another. Every screen changes to that business's invoices, purchases, expenses, receipts, recurring invoices, reports and returns. Manage profiles… opens Settings ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#notifications","p":"Getting around","s":"Notifications","t":"notifications\"> The bell shows a count of things that need you. Clicking it lists them, and clicking one takes you there: 🔁 recurring invoices created today ⚠ overdue invoices ⏰ invoices due in the next 3 days 📋 GST, TDS, TCS, advance tax and ITR dates in the next 10 days 📦 products low on stock Mark all as read clears the list. Anything new brings it back. The bell counts all your businesses together."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#command-palette","p":"Getting around","s":"Quick search: Ctrl + K","t":"command-palette\"> Press Ctrl + K anywhere, even while typing, and start typing. You can: go to any screen, or start a new invoice; open an invoice by its number or client; find a client by name or GSTIN, or a product by name or HSN, which opens their list; jump to Settings, switch dark mode, or see what is new in an update. Use ↑ ↓ and Enter . Esc closes it. Quick search finding a client and their invoices."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#keyboard","p":"Getting around","s":"Keyboard shortcuts","t":"keyboard\"> Ctrl + K Quick search Ctrl + N New invoice Ctrl + Shift + L Lock the app (when a PIN is set) Ctrl + / Show all shortcuts Esc Close a dialog Enter Confirm a dialog On the invoice screen there are more: see Keyboard shortcuts on this screen . On a Mac, use ⌘ instead of Ctrl ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#dark-mode","p":"Getting around","s":"Dark mode","t":"dark-mode\"> Dark Mode in the sidebar switches the app to dark colours, and Light Mode switches back. Invoices and PDFs always print in their normal colours."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#install-as-app","p":"Getting around","s":"Opening it like a desktop app","t":"install-as-app\"> In Chrome and Edge, the app may offer Install App . It then opens in its own window with its own icon, like any other program, and right-clicking the icon jumps straight to New Invoice or GST Returns. It is the same app and the same data."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#app-not-running","p":"Getting around","s":"\"Needs a Quick Start\"","t":"app-not-running\"> If the app's engine is not running, the page says Free GST Billing Software Needs a Quick Start . Your data is safe. Double-click Free GST Billing on your Desktop and click Open App ; the page carries on by itself once it is running."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Troubleshooting and questions","t":"The problems people run into most, what causes each one, and how to fix it."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#files-missing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The launcher says files are missing, or to extract the ZIP","t":"files-missing\"> The launcher was opened from inside the ZIP, or the ZIP was only partly extracted. Close it, right-click the ZIP, choose Extract All… , and open the launcher from the extracted folder. Keep the launcher and the _system folder together. See Extract the ZIP before opening anything ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#mac-blocked","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The Mac will not open the launcher","t":"mac-blocked\"> \"could not be executed because you do not have appropriate access privileges\" : open Terminal (Applications → Utilities), type chmod +x with a space after it, drag Free GST Billing - MAC into the Terminal window, press Enter, and open the file again. Downloads from v1.10.82 do not need this. \"cannot be opened because Apple cannot check it for malicious software\" or \"unidentified developer\" : the app is not signed by Apple. Hold Control , click Free GST Billing - MAC , choose Open , then Open again. Only the first time. Or use System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway . \""},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#windows-protected","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Windows blocked the launcher","t":"windows-protected\"> Click More info , then Run anyway . If it still will not open, right-click the launcher, choose Properties and tick Unblock . See \"Windows protected your PC\" ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#install-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The install stopped with an error","t":"install-failed\"> \"Could not download Node.js\" or \"could not install the app's dependencies\" : the first install needs the internet. Check the connection, or a work proxy or firewall, and click Install again. It carries on where it stopped. \"Node.js was downloaded but will not run\" : antivirus probably removed it. Add the app's folder to your antivirus exclusions, or install Node.js yourself from nodejs.org , then click Install again. \"The Node.js on this PC (v6...) is too old\" , npm ERR! , or a file named npm-debug.log in the _system folder: the PC has an old Node.js. From v1.10.81 the app set"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#not-answered","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Still starting...\" or \"The server has not answered in 90 seconds\"","t":"not-answered\"> The first start after an install or update is slow, because antivirus checks every new file. Wait a minute, then open http://localhost:47371 in your browser. If it still does not open, close the black window and click Open App again; from v1.10.81 it also repairs an install that an update left half done. If the window shows an error above that line, the entries under The install stopped with an error say what to do."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#cannot-connect","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Cannot connect\", a blank page, or \"Needs a Quick Start\"","t":"cannot-connect\"> The app is not running. Open the Free GST Billing shortcut and click Open App ; it starts the app if needed and opens the right address. You never need to type the address yourself; if its usual port is busy, the app picks another and the shortcut follows it."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#wrong-tax","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The invoice has the wrong tax split","t":"wrong-tax\"> Check your own state in Settings . Check the client's state , or their GSTIN, which fills the state in. If goods go to a different state from the client's address, set Place of Supply on the invoice. For a client abroad, set their country : it is then an export, charged as IGST. For an SEZ unit, tick SEZ on the client. See How GST is worked out ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#no-tax","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"No GST is charged at all","t":"no-tax\"> The Tax % column is probably turned off under Customize . Turning it off removes GST from the invoice, and your choice carries over to new invoices. Tick it again. Bills of supply and delivery challans never charge GST."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#missing-on-pdf","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Something is missing from the PDF","t":"missing-on-pdf\"> Logo, signature or stamp : check it is uploaded and saved in Settings , and ticked under Customize. UPI QR code : needs a UPI ID on the account, a rupee invoice, and UPI QR ticked under Customize. Bank details or PAN : tick Bank details under Customize; the account needs a bank name. Anything on a receipt printer : receipts leave some things out on purpose. See What a receipt leaves out ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gstr1-blocked","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"GSTR-1 export says \"blocked\"","t":"gstr1-blocked\"> An invoice number is too long or has characters the portal refuses, or an item has a GST rate the portal does not accept. The message names the first one. See Checks before the file is made ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#update-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"An update went wrong","t":"update-failed\"> Your data folder is never changed by an update, and a backup was saved in Documents\\FreeGSTBill Backups before it started. Run the update again, which fixes most problems. If it still fails, download the ZIP and extract it over the app folder by hand."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gst-labels","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"It says VAT instead of GST, or the other way round","t":"gst-labels\"> Change Region in Settings, and check your country in Company Details. Tax names follow the seller's country."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#ocr-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Reading a bill photo failed","t":"ocr-failed\"> Use a sharp, straight, well-lit JPG or PNG under 8 MB, cropped to the bill. If it still fails, reload the page with Ctrl + F5 and try again, or enter the bill by hand."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#other-devices","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Can I use it on my phone or another computer?","t":"other-devices\"> The app runs on the computer it is installed on, and only that computer can open it. It has no user accounts, so it is deliberately not shared over your network, where anyone connected could read your books. (The optional PIN lock locks the screen on this computer only.) To work on another computer, move your data there."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#internet","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Does it need the internet?","t":"internet\"> Only to install and to update. Invoices, reports, GST returns and even reading bills from photos all work offline. Google Drive upload uses the internet too."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#privacy","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Is my data sent anywhere?","t":"privacy\"> No. There is no account, no tracking and no server of ours. Your data stays in the app's folder unless you choose Google Drive, which copies files into your own Drive."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#report-problem","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Reporting a problem","t":"report-problem\"> Use the Report a problem form on GitHub. It asks for the version ( Settings, App Updates ), your computer, what you did and what you saw, and a screenshot (hide your GSTIN and bank details). If the app does not start, add what node -v and npm -v show in Command Prompt. Problems are fixed in the Saturday update , and anything urgent, such as the app not opening, straight away. For a new feature use Ask for a feature ."},{"u":"limitations.html","p":"What it does not do","s":"What the app does not do","t":"So you can plan around them: the things this app leaves to the government portals, your CA, or other tools."},{"u":"limitations.html#e-invoicing","p":"What it does not do","s":"E-invoicing (IRN and signed QR)","t":"e-invoicing\"> The app does not connect to the Invoice Registration Portal, so it cannot get an IRN or the signed QR code. If your turnover makes e-invoicing compulsory for you, generate the IRN on the IRP and keep it with the invoice."},{"u":"limitations.html#portal-filing","p":"What it does not do","s":"Filing returns for you","t":"portal-filing\"> It makes the GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B files and figures. It does not log in to the GST portal or file anything. You, or your CA, upload and file on gst.gov.in."},{"u":"limitations.html#eway-generation","p":"What it does not do","s":"Generating e-way bills","t":"eway-generation\"> It makes the file for the e-way bill portal. The e-way bill number itself is generated on the portal."},{"u":"limitations.html#not-in-gstr1","p":"What it does not do","s":"Things not in the GSTR-1 file","t":"not-in-gstr1\"> Exports (Table 6A) must be added on the portal with the shipping bill details. Nil-rated, exempt and non-GST supplies (Table 8), such as bills of supply, are not included. Debit notes are not supported as a document type. Advances received before invoicing are not tracked."},{"u":"limitations.html#accounting","p":"What it does not do","s":"Full accounting","t":"accounting\"> There is no double-entry ledger, balance sheet, trial balance, cash or bank book, bank reconciliation or journal entries yet. It covers invoicing, receivables, purchases, expenses, stock and GST. For the rest, give your CA the Excel or CSV exports."},{"u":"limitations.html#multi-user","p":"What it does not do","s":"Several people, or several computers","t":"multi-user\"> There are no user accounts or roles (an optional PIN can lock the screen), and the app only opens on the computer it runs on. One computer holds the books; see moving to a new computer ."},{"u":"limitations.html#income-tax-limits","p":"What it does not do","s":"Income tax","t":"income-tax-limits\"> The income tax helper estimates tax for FY 2025-26, for someone under 60. It does not file your return or produce the ITR file the portal takes. See Income tax helper ."},{"u":"limitations.html#stock-limits","p":"What it does not do","s":"Stock","t":"stock-limits\"> Stock is one count per product. There are no batches, expiry dates, serial numbers or warehouses. Stock is valued at purchase price in Reports, Stock ."},{"u":"glossary.html","p":"Glossary","s":"Glossary","t":"The GST and tax terms used in the app and in these pages, in plain words."},{"u":"glossary.html#terms","p":"Glossary","s":"Terms A to Z","t":"terms\"> Term Meaning AATO Annual aggregate turnover: your total sales in a year across all your GSTINs on one PAN. B2B / B2C Sales to a GST-registered business / to someone unregistered, such as a consumer. B2C Large An inter-state sale to an unregistered buyer above ₹1 lakh (₹2.5 lakh before 1 August 2024), reported invoice by invoice in GSTR-1. Bill of supply A bill without GST, for exempt goods or services, or from a composition dealer. CGST, SGST, UTGST, IGST Central, State and Union Territory GST are charged together on a sale within one state or territory. Integrated GST is charged on a "},{"u":"support.html","p":"Support & About","s":"Support & About","t":"Who makes Free GST Billing, how you can help it grow, and what OM RAJ builds for businesses."},{"u":"support.html#about","p":"Support & About","s":"Free, and it stays free","t":"about\"> Free GST Billing is built and maintained by @omraj in India. No ads, no account, no locked features, and your invoices never leave your computer. The full source code is on GitHub under the MIT licence. If it saves you time every month, you can help keep the fixes and new features coming."},{"u":"support.html#upi","p":"Support & About","s":"Support with UPI QR","t":"upi\"> Scan with GPay, PhonePe, Paytm, BHIM, SBI or any UPI app. Any amount helps keep updates coming. Scan with any UPI app to support ongoing open-source development."},{"u":"support.html#supporters","p":"Support & About","s":"Supporters","t":"supporters\" class=\"supporters\" hidden>"},{"u":"support.html#free-ways","p":"Support & About","s":"Help without paying","t":"free-ways\"> These matter just as much. Star it on GitHub : helps other businesses find it. Tell another business : send it to a friend on WhatsApp. Report a bug or ask for a feature : many features started as a request."},{"u":"support.html#weekly","p":"Support & About","s":"A new update every Saturday","t":"weekly\"> Every Saturday we release one update with that week's fixes and new features. The app tells you when it is ready: click Update in the sidebar, and your invoices and settings are kept. Anything urgent, such as the app not opening, is fixed straight away. Report a problem : say which version, which computer, and what you did. That lets us fix it the same week. Ask for a feature : we read every request each week, and the ones most people ask for come first. Add a 👍 to an open request to vote for it. You get a reply on GitHub when it ships. What each update changed is in the app under Su"},{"u":"support.html#services","p":"Support & About","s":"Work with OM RAJ","t":"services\"> The developer behind this app builds software for businesses too. Custom software & web apps Websites, web apps and business tools built for how you work. Customising this app Your own invoice layout, reports or features in Free GST Billing. Setup & data migration Installation, moving your data from Tally or Excel, and training. Support plans for businesses Priority help and updates on a yearly plan. AI integration Add AI to your product: assistants, document reading, smart search. AI automation Automate the repetitive work in the software you already use. Mobile apps Android and iP"},{"u":"support.html#in-the-app","p":"Support & About","s":"In the app","t":"in-the-app\"> The same page is in the app: Support & About , near the bottom of the sidebar. See Getting around for the thank-you card and the GitHub star note."}];
